hadiths[1002]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16033","(16033) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, on the authority of Al-Murqi’, on the authority of Abu Dharr, who said: No one has the right to He performs Hajj and then makes it an Umrah except for the passengers who were with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"16034","(16034) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Mujahid, he said: Ibn al-Zubayr said: Spread the Hajj alone and leave the saying This blinded you, and this reached Ibn Abbas, and he said: Indeed, the one whose heart and eyes God has blinded, why do you not ask your mother? So he asked her, and she said: We came with the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, as pilgrims, so he commanded us, and we made all of the lawful things lawful until the censers glowed bright. Between men and women. (Ahmad 6/344, Tabarani 244)"
"16035","(16035) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Malik narrated to us, on the authority of Ata, who said regarding the bath of the Sacred Mosque: When they go out of The sanctuary, so take it if you wish."
"16036","(16036) Zayd bin Harun told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, he said: It was not He sees harm in hunting the doves of the Sanctuary if they leave the Sanctuary."
"16037","(16037) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’ and Tawoos, who said about a man who circumambulated eight times. He said: He mentioned it before he prayed two rak'ahs, circumambulated six times, and prayed four rak'ahs, and if he mentioned it after he prayed He performed two rak'ahs, circumambulated six times, then prayed two rak'ahs, and if he wished, he did not need to do that."
"16038","(16038) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: When he circumambulates the Kaaba, eight Rounds of prayer, pray two rak'ahs."
"16039","(16039) Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abi Ismail Al-Sulami, who said: Saeed bin Jubayr was asked about Dates for the person in ihram, so he said: What’s wrong with them? He said, “It contains animals.” He said, “Eat dates, but do not eat animals.”"
"16040","(16040) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Ala’ bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Al-Hakam and Hammad in Muharram, Yatwashah, he hated it. One of them did not see any harm in him."
"16041","(16041) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’ who was asked about a man who circumambulated six days and prayed. Two rak'ahs? He said: He performs another circumambulation and prays two rak'ahs."
"16042","(16042) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Bishr ibn Mansour, on the authority of Shuaib, who said: Al-Hasan was asked about a man who circumambulated six days? He said: Perform another circumambulation."
"16043","(16043) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ubaid al-Muttab, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If you receive the stone, say: No. There is no god but Allah, and Allah is the greatest."
"16044","(16044) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Musa bin Ubaidah, on the authority of Wahhab bin Wahhab, on the authority of Sa`id bin al-Musayyab, on the authority of Omar, When he received peace, he used to say: I believe in God and disbelieve in the tyrant."
"16045","(16045) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Masoudi, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, who said: When Ali received the stone, he would say: Oh God In confirmation of Your Book and the Sunnah of Your Prophet."
"16046","(16046) Zaid bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Masoudi, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali, a similar hadith Waki’, on the authority of Al-Masoudi."
"16047","(16047) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad ibn Zayd, on the authority of Kathir ibn Shanzir, on the authority of Ata`, who said: If you receive the stone So kiss your hands, and do not vote with a kiss."
"16048","(16048) Yahya bin Sa’id narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, that it was It is desirable that there not be anything under the juliqin."
"16049","(16049) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Khalid Al-A’war, he said: Dhar Al-Hamdani disagreed with me regarding Hajj on Ali. Which one is better? Dhar said: Al-Mahmal. He said: So I asked Abraham, and he said: Al-Qatab."
"16050","(16050) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Ishaq bin Sa`id al-Qurashi narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that he saw A companion from the people of Yemen, the people of Adam, and he said: Whoever likes to look at something similar to the companions of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace. May the peace and blessings of God be upon him, let him look at these people."
"16051","(16051) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-Umari narrated to us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that he used to perform Hajj on a journey."
"16052","(16052) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Fudayl bin Iyadh narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawus, who said: The Hajj of the righteous is on mounts."
"16053","(16053) Waki’ told us, he said: Rabi’ told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Aban, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, he said: The Messenger of God performed Hajj. God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was on a saddle and a piece of cotton was worth it, or he said: It is not worth anything except four dirhams, then he said: Oh God. A Hajj in which there is neither hypocrisy nor hearing. (Tirmidhi 334, Ibn Majah 2890)"
"16054","(16054) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Sinan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Harith, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him He greeted Hajj on a saddle, and he shook, and said: He passed, and he moved forward, and said: Here you go. Indeed, the life is the life of the hereafter."
"16055","(16055) Qurayh bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: It was disliked to perform Hajj on a burden, and he would say: It is only People used to perform Hajj by groups and travelers."
"16056","(16056) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: If he bids farewell, he should not do any work until He goes out to Al-Abtah, and when he goes out to Al-Abtah, he says: There is no harm in him performing the prayer."
"16057","(16057) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Zayd, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Abdullah bin Abi Mughith, that Omar bin Abdul Aziz bid farewell, then a man from Quraysh came and greeted him, so he repeated the farewell."
"16058","(16058) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of a man whom he did not name, on the authority of Omar bin Abdul Aziz, that he bid farewell So he wrote a letter and repeated his farewell."
"16059","(16059) Hakam al-Razi narrated to us, saying: I heard a man asking Humayd what Al-Hasan’s saying was, or Al-Hasan’s opinion of a man when he bid farewell. ? He said: He saw nothing wrong with it being offered to him if he bought it."
"16060","(16060) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Khalid, that Abu Qalab met a man who had come from Umrah, and he said: Be righteous in your work, be righteous. Work"
"16061","(16061) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Malik, who said: Talhah met Hammad, and he said: Accomplish your sacrifice."
"16062","(16062) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of someone who heard Ibn Umar say to the pilgrim when he came: May God accept your sacrifice. And He will increase your reward and spare your expenses."
"16063","(16063) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Yahya bin Ubaid, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abd Allah bin Al-Sa'ib said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying between the pillar and the stone: {Our Lord, give us in this world. Good, and in the Hereafter, good, and protect us from the torment of the Fire. (Abu Dawud 1887. Ahmad 3/411)"
"16064","(16064) Asbat bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, he said: It was one of the supplications of Ibn Abbas who did not He leaves between the corner and the Maqam to say: My Lord, satisfy me with what You have provided for me, and bless me therein, and grant success to all in my absence. I am fine

(Ibn Khuzaymah 2728)"
"16065","(16065) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ishaq, on the authority of an old woman from the people of Mecca, who said: Ibn Affan was afflicted. When I was fourteen years old, she said: I saw the house, and there was no clothing on it, except what the people covered it with. The red garment is thrown upon him, and the white garment, and the woolen garment, and whatever he is clothed with are hung on him. I saw him, and there was no gold or silver on him. Muhammad said: The House was not covered during the time of Abu Bakr. Nor Omar, and Omar bin Abdul Aziz covered Al-Wasail and Al-Qabatiya, and Al-Wasail were Yemeni clothes."
"16066","(16066) Surayj bin Al-Nu’man told us, he said: Falih told us, on the authority of Nafi’, he said: Ibn Umar used to glorify his body before he The Kaaba is covered with jewels, patterns, and robes, then he takes it off before he slaughters it and sends it to his storeroom. He covered the Kaaba for the Kaaba, but when the Kaaba was covered, he left that."
"16067","(16067) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Hasan, on the authority of Laith, who said: The Ka’b was covered during the time of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May the peace and blessings of God be upon him and grant him peace."
"16068","(16068) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: When they visited a sick person, they would not perform Hajj. He slaughters his body."
"16069","(16069) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: They used to prefer it if it was not Hajj is to bequeath a gift."
"16070","(16070) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Jabir, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, recited In the two rak'ahs of circumambulation (Say, O disbelievers) and (Say: He is Allah, One). (Tirmidhi 869. Ahmad 3/320)"
"16071","(16071) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Musa bin Ubaidah, on the authority of Yaqoub bin Zaid, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace In the two rak'ahs of Tawaf, he recited (Say, O disbelievers) and (Say: He is Allah, One)."
"16072","(16072) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of a person giving in Muharram that strikes a monkey. He said: He is judged. Aliyah"
"16073","(16073) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him And he entered Mecca from the highest place."
"16074","(16074) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: I do not care if I enter from Below Mecca"
"16075","(16075) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Umari, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was It enters from the upper fold and exits from the lower fold. (Bukhari 1576, Muslim 918)"
"16076","(16076) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was When he exits, he exits by the tree’s path, and when he enters, he enters by the Ma’aras path, and when he enters Makkah, he enters by the upper gates. And when it comes out, it comes out of the lower fold. (Bukhari 1533. Muslim 918)"
"16077","(16077) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Nasr bin Adiy, who said: I heard Mujahid say: The ancient house was called because of its He has been freed from the tyrants, for there is no tyrant who claims to be his."
"16078","(16078) Waki’, Ghandar, and Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Al-Hikam, on the authority of Ikrimah, ‘Ata’, and Tawoos: {So make your hearts Among the people are those who have turned to Him. They said: To Him their hearts have turned. They come to Him, meaning the House."
"16079","(16079) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abu al-Haytham, on the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr: {God made the Ka`b The Sacred House as an establishment for the people. He said: Strengthening their religion."
"16080","(16080) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, he said: It was named The Kaaba because it is square, but it was called the body because of the fat people."
"16081","(16081) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ghalib, on the authority of Sa`id ibn Jubayr: {And when We made the House a place of return for the people} He said: They will perform Hajj, then they will return."
"16082","(16082) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Malik ibn Mughal, on the authority of Ata’, who said: They will perform Hajj for him, but they will not make up for a period of time from him."
"16083","(16083) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Had he not said: {So make your hearts better than the people} it would have been crowded. On him are Persians and Romans."
"16084","(16084) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, he said: They are called the days of the sunrise. They were shining in the sun."
"16085","(16085) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Aslam al-Munqari, who said: I said to Ata’: I will go out to Medina as my family. Omrah from the appointed time of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace? He said: Your circumambulation of the Kaaba is more beloved to me than your travel to Medina."
"16086","(16086) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Amr bin Dharr narrated to us, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Your circumambulation of the Kaaba is more beloved to me than your travel. To Medina"
"16087","(16087) Ismail bin Abdul-Malik told us, on the authority of Ata’, who said: Circumambulating the Kaaba is more beloved to me than going out for the Umrah."
"16088","(16088) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: It was called Al-Ma’tiya because they were They enjoy women and clothes."
"16089","(16089) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Uthman, on the authority of a man, who said: I saw Shaybah took whatever he had fallen from the covering of the Ka’bah and put it among the poor. Sufyan said: There is no harm in buying it from the poor. If He gave it to them."
"16090","(16090) Shazan narrated to us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Al-Hakam bin Utaiba, he said: It was It is desirable or recommended to wash on the days of Tashreeq if one goes to the mosque, or to the pebbles."
"16091","(16091) Abu Asama told us, he said: I heard Sufyan being asked about someone who converted to Islam and performed Hajj, then apostatized, then returned to Islam, and it is obligatory for him to perform Hajj. Does she have to perform Hajj or is that Hajj sufficient? He said: If he reverts to disbelief and destroys everything that came before him, then he must perform Hajj, and that should not be taken into account."
"16092","(16092) Ibn Yaman told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, Ata’, and Tawoos, who said: Glory be to Him. Any color you want."
"16093","(16093) Ibn Yaman told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ismail ibn Umayyah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that he said: In style"
"16094","(16094) Azhar told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that he used to exalt his body with such majesty. The families"
"16095","(16095) Ibn Yaman told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, that Abdul Rahman bin Awf: He was glorified with ink."
"16096","(16096) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Nafi’, who said: I heard Al-Hasan bin Muslim ask Tawoos about the lizard and the lizard. Will the Muhrim kill him? He said: There is no harm in it."
"16097","(16097) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: I asked Ata’ about a gecko being killed in the Sacred Mosque? He said: If he hurts you, there is no problem with him."
"16098","(16098) Hafs told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: Kill the gecko in the lawful and the sacred."
"16099","(16099) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shibl ibn Abbad, on the authority of Qays ibn Sa’d, on the authority of Tawus, that he hated being imprisoned in Mecca. He said: The house of torment should not be in the house of mercy."
"16100","(16100) Waki’ told us, he said: I asked Sufyan about a man who forgot to perform the obligatory Tawaf so he performed Tawaf al-Sadr, then he departed. ? So Sufyan said: Tawaf al-Sadr is obligatory, and he must pay blood for Tawaf al-Sadr, and he said: Al-Hasan bin Salih: It is not sufficient. It is as if he had not performed tawaf, and about a qarin who came and circumambulated for Hajj before Umrah. He said: He makes the tawaf that he did for Hajj count for Umrah. He must perform the Tawaf of Hajj, and he said: Al-Hasan bin Salih: It is not sufficient."
"16101","(16101) I heard Wakee’, who said: I heard Sufyan saying: If forgetfulness, talbiyah, and takbeer are combined, he begins By forgetfulness, then the Talbiyah, then the takbeer."
"16102","(16102) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, that he said: There is a government in Sindhi chicken."
"16103","(16103) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of a giver among the slaves who enjoys enjoyment. He said: His master will slaughter a sheep on his behalf."
"16104","(16104) Abdul Salam told us, on the authority of Laith, he said: Ata, a peacock, and Mujahid saw me walking around the shrine and they turned away."
"16105","(16105) Abdul Salam bin Harb told us, on the authority of Malik bin Dinar, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: I saw him with a palm tree in his hand. And he drives away the pigeons of Mecca with it."
"16106","(16106) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus bin Mismar, who said: I saw a giving man and he mentioned something similar to it."
"16107","(16107) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ubaid al-Mukhtab, on the authority of a mujahid who was hunting and entered the sanctuary. Then he slaughtered it, and he said: There is no harm in it."
"16108","(16108) Al-Muharbibi narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Suqi, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: A pilgrim of the House of God is written on the night of Destiny is in their names and the names of their fathers, so none of them departs from them, and none of them increases."
"16109","(16109) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, who said: There is no harm in a person who is in a state of impurity reciting the prayer."
"16110","(16110) Ibn Abi Zaydah narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: He said: Be kind in every situation."
"16111","(16111) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: There is no harm in giving away a body of precious stones."
"16112","(16112) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: He is subject to the reward and the value of what he ate if He was given a reward, then he ate from it."
"16113","(16113) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Tariq bin Abdul Rahman, who said: I heard Ibn Abi Awfa being asked, about The man borrows money and performs Hajj? He said: May God provide for him, but he will not perform Hajj."
"16114","(16114) Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Suqi, on the authority of Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, that he used to borrow and perform Hajj. It was said to him: Do you borrow and perform Hajj? He said: Hajj is the fulfillment of the religion."
"16115","(16115) Ibn Uyaynah, peace be upon him, Ibn Suqi, told us on the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Munkadir, who said: Hajj is the fulfillment of the debt."
"16116","(16116) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, who said: Al-Hakam and our companions used to say that in Muharram, it is Sores on his body and head, can he treat them with perfume? They said: There are two expiations in it, an expiation for his head and an expiation for his body."
"16117","(16117) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, who said: He must pay one expiation."
"16118","(16118) Hatim bin Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of his father, who said: Ali said: Whoever is forced to wear a garment while he is in ihram, He had nothing but a cloak, so let him drape it, make the top of it the bottom, then let him put it on."
"16119","(16119) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’, and Mujahid, who said: The ihram may not enter His shoulders are in the cloak, and there is no harm in him wearing it."
"16120","(16120) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The person in ihram should not put his shoulders into the cloaks, and there is no problem. To wear it."
"16121","(16121) Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he did not see any harm in a pilgrim in ihram wearing the Qubbāyah, unless He puts his shoulder into it."
"16122","(16122) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abu Muslimama, who said: Ikrimah was asked about a muhrim who wore an hood, and he said: He takes it off."
"16123","(16123) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Juma’, on the authority of Abu Salama, that Omar bin Al-Khattab and Aisha When they arrived in Mecca, they had not reached the place from which they had migrated."
"16124","(16124) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, who said: Whenever Abd al-Rahman bin Awf came He came to Mecca as a pilgrim who hated to stay in the house from which he had emigrated."
"16125","(16125) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ikrimah ibn Ammar, on the authority of Taysala, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that he revealed Al-Arak with his knowledge."
"16126","(16126) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Masoud."
"16127","(16127) Hatim bin Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Jabir, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace"
"16128","(16128) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that menstruation came By knowledge"
"16129","(16129) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, saying: Abu Mawdud narrated to me, saying: Zayd ibn Abdullah ibn Qusayt narrated to me, He said: I saw a group of the Companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, when the mosque was left for them, they stood up to the pomegranates of the pulpit, which had been knocked down. So they wiped them off and called. He said: And I saw Yazid doing that."
"16130","(16130) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Yazid Al-Laythi, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, he hated to put his hand on the pulpit."
"16131","(16131) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Thabit bin Qais, who said: I saw Abu Bakr, when he rose on the pulpit, he took off his Her shoes"
"16132","(16132) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Malik, he said: Al-Zuhri was asked: Does a woman imitate or feel? He said: There is no harm in it."
"16133","(16133) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Hilal, who said: I saw Omar bin Abdul Aziz when he went up to the pulpit of the Prophet. May God bless him and grant him peace. He took off his shoes."
"16134","(16134) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Mahdi, he said: Shuaib bin Al-Habhab told me, he said: I heard Al-Sha’bi say: God made these rituals to atone for them the sins of the children of Adam."
"16135","(16135) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: I said to him: How does he push the cattle? He said: How did you make it easy?"
"16136","(16136) Ishaq bin Mansour narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, that he disliked the ihram if he passed by. With a fragrant scent, he puts his garment over his nose and holds it."
"16137","(16137) Ishaq bin Mansour told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Ata’, who said: There is no harm in him."
"16138","(16138) Ishaq bin Mansour told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’, Tawoos, and Mujahid. They said: There is no harm in him."
"16139","(16139) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: I said to Ata’: A man threw a heel and did not shave. Did the people shave? ? He said: Yes."
"16140","(16140) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, that he disliked selling his hair if he shaved it. It means the forbidden."
"16141","(16141) Sufyan bin Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, who said about every woman with a stomach, a sheep."
"16142","(16142) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: “Every person with a belly is a sheep.”"
"16143","(16143) Ruh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Adni, who said: I saw Muhammad ibn Ali sand between The Yemeni corner and the stone, which is flat."
"16144","(16144) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ibn Ali, on the authority of his father, he said: I saw the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, circumambulating the Kaaba lying down. (Abu Dawud 1878. Ahmad 4/223)"
"16145","(16145) Qubaisa narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Abdul Hamid, on the authority of Ibn Ali, on the authority of his father, On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"16146","(16146) Qubaisa narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, that Omar bin Abdul Aziz walked around the Kaaba lying down."
"16147","(16147) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Imran bin Hudayr, on the authority of Abu Majlis, in his saying: (The wild game is forbidden to you as long as you Haram) He said: Whatever lives on land and sea, do not stop it, and if it lives in the sea, then do not stop it."
"16148","(16148) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Sa’id al-Tamar, who said: I saw Ibn al-Hanafi sitting on a red mattress, and he Muharram."
"16149","(16149) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: There is no harm in him sitting on the bed. Dyeed with saffron, which is forbidden."
"16150","(16150) Muadh bin Muadh told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: There is no harm in him."
"16151","(16151) Muadh bin Muadh told us, he said: Ibn Aoun told us, he said: I was informed, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that he was reluctant to The pilgrim in ihram sits on the bed dyed with saffron."
"16152","Abu Abdul Rahman Buqiy bin Mukhlid told us, he said: Abu Bakr Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Abi Shayba told us, he said:

(16152) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Maymun Abi al-Mughalis, on the authority of Abu Najih, who said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Whoever is able to get married and does not get married is not one of us. (Abu Dawud 2020, Abdul Razzaq 10376)"
"16153","(16153) Ibn Al-Mubarak narrated to us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab: On the authority of Sa’d, that the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He responded to Uthman bin Maz’un’s celibacy, and if he had given him permission, he would have chosen us. (Muslim 1020, Ahmad 1/176)"
"16154","(16154) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamiya, who said: I was walking with Abdullah in Manna, Then Othman met him, and he stood with him and spoke to him. Othman said to him: O Abu Abdul Rahman, should I not marry you to my young maid, perhaps she will Does it remind you of some of your past time? Then Abdullah said: If you say that, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to us: O young men, whoever is able Whoever among you is unable to do so, let him get married, for it will make one look better, and whoever is not able to do so should fast, for it will be a reward for him. (Bukhari 50650 Muslim 1018)"
"16155","(16155) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ammar bin Umair, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Zayd, on the authority of Abd God said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to us: O young men, whoever of you can marry, let him get married. For it lowers the gaze and improves chastity, and whoever is not able to do so should fast, for it is a reward for him. (Bukhari 5066. Muslim 1019)"
"16156","(16156) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Raja’i, on the authority of Uthman bin Khalid, on the authority of Al-Zuhri: on the authority of Shaddad bin Aws, He had lost his sight and said: Marry me, for the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, has commanded me not to meet God single."
"16157","(16157) Muhammad bin Bishr told us, on the authority of Abu Raja’, on the authority of Al-Hakam bin Zayd, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: Muadh said during his illness The day he died: Marry me, for I hate to meet God single."
"16158","(16158) Sufyan bin Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Misra, who said: Tawoos said to me: You may marry, or I will tell you what Omar said to Abu al-Zawaid: Nothing prevents you from getting married except inability or immorality."
"16159","(16159) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Hujayr, on the authority of Tawus, who said: A young man’s ritual rite is not complete until he gets married."
"16160","(16160) Abbad bin Awwam told us, on the authority of Sufyan bin Hussein, on the authority of Abul Hakam Sayyar, on the authority of Abi Wael, on the authority of Ibn Masoud said: If I had not lived, or if I had only been in this world for ten days, I would have loved to have a woman with me in them."
"16161","(16161) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwah, on the authority of his father, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: : Marry women, for they will give you money."
"16162","(16162) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn al-Muntashir, who said: Omar said, “Seek wealth in The curse"
"16163","(16163) Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ibrahim ibn Misra, on the authority of Tawoos, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Peace and blessings of God be upon him: He has not seen anything like marriage for those who love each other. (Bayhaqi 78)"
"16164","(16164) Abdullah narrated to us, saying: Israel narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Zayd, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: If not Only one night will remain of eternity. I would love to have a woman with me that night."
"16165","(16165) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Qays, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: We were with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. When we were young, we said, O Messenger of God, shall we not ask him to be castrated? He said: No, then he gave us permission to marry a woman with a garment for a specified period, then Abdullah recited: “O you who have believed, do not deprive Good things that God has made lawful for you.

(Bukhari 4615. Muslim 11)"
"16166","(16166) A friend of ours, nicknamed Abu Bakr, narrated to us. He said: Ibn Hisham al-Dastawwi narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Samarra: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade celibacy. (Tirmidhi 1082. Ahmad 5/17)"
"16167","(16167) Muadh narrated to us, saying: Ibn Juraij informed us, on the authority of Sulaiman bin Musa, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whatever woman is not married to her guardian or guardians. Her marriage is invalid, so her marriage is invalid. They said it three times. If he agrees with her, then she gets her dowry for what he agrees with her. If they quarrel. The Sultan is the guardian of those who have no guardian. (Abu Dawud 2076. Ahmad 6/165)"
"16168","(16168) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of a nephew of Ubaid ibn Umair, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Ma`abad that Umar Refusal of the marriage of a woman who was married without the permission of her guardian."
"16169","(16169) Hafs told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawoos, on the authority of Omar, who said: There is no marriage except with a guardian."
"16170","(16170) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: None of the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He was more severe in marriage without a guardian than Ali, to the point that he used to hit her."
"16171","(16171) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Khathim, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: There is no marriage except A guardian, or a guiding authority."
"16172","(16172) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shuabi, he said: I heard Al-Waffah, he said: I heard Jabir bin Zaid saying: There is no marriage except with a guardian. And you are witnesses."
"16173","(16173) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: There is no marriage except with a guardian."
"16174","(16174) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he used to say: There is no marriage except with a guardian, or a sultan."
"16175","(16175) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: A woman should not be married except with the permission of her guardian. If she does not have a guardian, then the Sultan."
"16176","(16176) Zaid narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of his companions, on the authority of Ibrahim, the same."
"16177","(16177) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, on the authority of Uthman ibn Al-Aswad, on the authority of Amr ibn Abi Sufyan, who said: Omar said: Do not marry A woman is married except with the permission of her guardian, even if she has had ten sexual intercourse, or with the permission of a ruler."
"16178","(16178) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Ibn Sirin in the mirror from the people of Al-Sawad. She has no guardian. He said: Al-Hasan is the Sultan, and Ibn Sirin said: A man from among the Muslims."
"16179","(16179) Abdullah bin Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Ubaidah, on the authority of Ibrahim and Al-Shu’abi, who said: A woman should not be married except with permission. Her guardian, and her guardian shall not marry her except with her permission."
"16180","(16180) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawus, who said: A woman was brought to Umar who had become pregnant, and she said: Marry me. With testimony from my mother and sister, he separated them and averted the punishment from them, and said: There is no marriage except with a guardian."
"16181","(16181) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali, who said: No marriage. Except with a guardian, and there is no marriage except with witnesses."
"16182","(16182) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, who said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: There is no marriage except with a guardian, and the Sultan is the guardian of one who has no guardian. (Ahmad 1/250, Ibn Majah 1880)"
"16183","(16183) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Yazid, he said: I heard Al-Hasan say: There is no marriage except with a guardian and a witness. Justly and truthfully with known people, witnesses and publicity."
"16184","(16184) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of his father, who said: I said to Al-Hassan, “She is a slave girl from the people of the earth, meaning she has no master.” A man proposed to her, and a man from her neighbors married her off. He said: She comes to the prince. He said: She is weaker than that. He said: So speak. A man was speaking to the prince. He said: Is she weaker than that? He said: I only know that. He said: I said to him: So the judge? He said: So the judge, except that he makes the judge cheap."
"16185","(16185) Affan told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Ziyad, who said: If the guardian and mother agree They get married, and if they disagree, then the guardian."
"16186","(16186) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Burda, on the authority of his father, he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: There is no marriage except with a guardian. (Abu Dawud 2078. Ahmed 394)"
"16187","(16187) Muawiyah bin Hisham told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Yahya, on the authority of a man called Al-Hakam bin Mina, on the authority of Ibn Abbas: The minimum number of people in a marriage is four: the one who marries, the one who gets married, and two witnesses."
"16188","(16188) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Burda, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: No. Marriage except with a guardian."
"16189","(16189) Abd al-Rahman bin Muhammad al-Muharbi narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar that he wanted to get married. So he and a man left, and the guardian and a man came."
"16190","(16190) Waki’, or someone else, narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The lowest thing is in There are four types of marriage: the one who marries, the one who is given in marriage, and two witnesses."
"16191","(16191) Ismail Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ikrimah Ibn Khalid, who said: You gathered the road into a path, so you made A married woman among them took her wife to a man from among the people other than her guardian, and a man married her to her. He said: So the age of the one who married her was flogged. And the one who was married and separated between them."
"16192","(16192) Abu Dawud al-Talisi narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad ibn Salama, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab, and al-Hasan in A woman got married without the permission of her guardian. He said: They will be separated. Al-Qasim bin Muhammad said: If the guardians allow it. It is permissible."
"16193","(16193) Abu Dawud told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Mus’ab, who said: I asked Abraham about a woman who married someone else. I was silent, and I asked Salim bin Abi Al-Ja’d, and he said: It is not permissible."
"16194","(16194) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: If a woman is married without a guardian, then The guardian permitted, permitted."
"16195","(16195) Muhammad bin Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Bakr, who said: A woman married without a guardian or clear evidence. So he wrote to Omar, and he wrote that she should be flogged for a hundred times, and he wrote to Al-Amsar, saying: “Any woman who marries without a guardian will be flogged.” In the position of an adulteress."
"16196","(16196) Muawiyah bin Hisham narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of a man from the people of the island, on the authority of Omar bin Abd. Al-Aziz said that a man married a woman and she had a guardian, and he had more right than him on the path of the Romans, so Omar rejected the marriage and said: The guardian or else The Sultan."
"16197","(16197) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of his mother, on the authority of Bahri bint Hani’, who said: She married Al-Qaqa’. Ibn Shur asked me and made for me a turban made of jewellery, on the condition that he stay with me for the night. So he stayed overnight, and I put a burr in it for him. He was a good-natured person, and he woke up feeling overwhelmed with good-naturedness, so he said to me: You have exposed me, and I said to him: Is there a secret like me? Then Ubayy, one of the Bedouins, came and attacked Ali. Ali said to Al-Qaqa’: Have you entered? He said: Yes, so he permitted the marriage."
"16198","(16198) Abu Dawud narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bai, on the authority of Mus’ab, who said: I asked Musa bin Abdullah bin Zayd, and he said: It is permissible. In the case of a woman, marriage without a guardian."
"16199","(16199) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, who said: I asked Al-Zuhri about a woman who married without a guardian, and he said: If Competent, permissible."
"16200","(16200) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ismail bin Salem, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: If he is competent, he will be permitted."
"16201","(16201) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Abu Qais Al-Awdi, on the authority of the one who narrated to him, on the authority of Ali, that he permitted The marriage of a woman without a guardian. Her mother married her off with her consent."
"16202","(14202) Salam and Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Aziz bin Rafi’, on the authority of Abu Salma bin Abd al-Rahman, who said: She came A woman went to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and she said: O Messenger of God, my son’s uncle proposed to me, but my father turned him around and married me off. And I hate him. He said: So he called her father and asked him about that. He said: I married her and I did not treat her with anything good. So the Messenger of God said: God, may God bless him and grant him peace: There is no marriage for you. Go and marry whomever you wish. (Abdul Razzaq 10303)"
"16203","(14203) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, that Al-Qasim bin Muhammad informed him that Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid and Mujma` bin Yazid from the Ansari told him that a man among them called Khudham had married his son to him. She disliked marrying her father, so she went to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and mentioned that to him, so he annulled the marriage. Ubayyah, so she got engaged and married Abu Lubabah ibn Abd al-Mundhir, and Yahya mentioned that he heard that she was Dressed (Bukhari 5139. Abu Dawud 2094)"
"16204","(16204) Zaid bin Harun narrated to us, saying: Yahya bin Saeed narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Muhammad, that Aisha got married. Hafsah Ibn Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Bakr al-Mundhir bin al-Zubayr and Abd al-Rahman were absent, so when Abd al-Rahman came he became angry and said: O servants of God, someone like me is the one who spreads crumbs on his daughters? Aisha got angry and said: I want, on the authority of Al-Mundhir."
"16205","(14205) Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Qais, on the authority of Huzayl, who said: It was raised to Ali. A woman was married off by her maternal uncle and mother. He said: So Ali permitted the marriage. He said: Sufyan said: It is not permissible because he is not a guardian. He said: Ali bin Saleh: It is permissible because when Ali permitted it, he was in the position of a guardian."
"16206","(16206) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Hakam, who said: When a man who had married a woman was brought before him, Ali Without a guardian, he entered into the marriage with her."
"16207","(14207) Muhammad bin Fudail told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The contract is not in the hands of women, but the contract is in the hands of men."
"16208","(14208) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim, who said: I do not know him except, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The boy was one of her brother’s sons. When the girl was one of her brother’s daughters, she put a cover between them and talked. Then, when nothing remains except marriage, she says: O so-and-so, marry me, for women do not marry."
"16209","(14209) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Muhammad, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: A woman should not marry another woman."
"16210","(16210) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: A woman should not marry another woman."
"16211","(16211) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: A woman may marry her slave woman, but if she frees her, she is not to be married to her."
"16212","(16212) Zaid bin Harun told us: Ibn Abi Dhib informed me, on the authority of the mawla of Banu Hashim, on the authority of Ali, who said : A woman shall not bear witness, meaning engagement, nor shall she be married."
"16213","(14213) Ghassan bin Mudar narrated to us, on the authority of Saeed bin Zaid, who said: A woman came to Jabir bin Zaid, and she said: I I got myself married, and he said: Are you telling me that you committed adultery? Then it blew and then set off."
"16214","(16214) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: A woman should not marry herself, and they used to say: The adulteress is the one who marries herself."
"16215","(14215) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Sirin, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, with a similar story."
"16216","(16216) Zayd ibn Harun told us: Sa`id informed us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Jabir ibn Zayd, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, He said: The prostitutes who marry themselves without your consent."
"16217","(16217) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ibn Abi Maliki, on the authority of Abu Amr Mawla. Aisha, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Women should be left in their private parts. She said: I said: The Messenger of God, indeed, they are ashamed. He said: The mother-in-law has more right to herself, and the virgin should be appointed to her, so her fasting is her consent. (Bukhari) 6946. Muslim 65)"
"16218","(16218) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq and Malik bin Anas, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Fadl, on the authority of Nafi’ bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: The noble woman has more right to herself than her guardian, and the virgin Her silence seeks her recognition. (Tirmidhi 1108 and Abu Dawud 2091)"
"16219","(16219) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: Whenever the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, would propose to someone One of his daughters sat next to her room and said: So-and-so is proposing to so-and-so. If she remains silent about him, he will marry her, and if she stabs him with her hand Hafs pointed with his index hand, meaning he stabbed her thigh, saying, “He did not marry her.” (Abdul Razzaq 10279. Bazzar 1421)"
"16220","(16220) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Al-Hakam, he said: Ali said: A man should not marry his daughter until he takes her as a consort."
"16221","(16221) Fudayl bin Iyad narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If the woman is among her father’s family He did not take her as a wife, even if she was not among his dependents, he would take her as a wife if he wanted to marry her."
"16222","(14222) Abduh bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: A man takes his daughter as his wife’s consent to marry a virgin. And the married man."
"16223","(16223) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he used to say: It is permissible for a father to marry his daughter. Whether he was a virgin, or married, whether she disliked it or did not dislike it."
"16224","(16224) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, who said: A man should not hate his daughter. The married man is forced to marry him."
"16225","(16225) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Malik ibn Anas, who said: Al-Qasim and Salem used to say: If Abu Bakr marries the virgin It is necessary for her, even if she dislikes it."
"16226","(16226) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: Abu al-Bakr invited her to a man, and she called him to him. Another, he said: He follows her desires if there is no harm in it, and if the one who invited her to him is her father, he will be happy with friendship. I am afraid that this will happen to her, but if her father forces her to do so, then he has more right."
"16227","(16227) A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amer, who said: No one is forced to marry except the father."
"16228","(14228) Affan told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Ikrimah; When Othman bin Affan wanted to marry one of his daughters, he would sit in her room and say, “So-and-so mentions you.”"
"16229","(16229) Amr ibn Muhammad narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim ibn Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, who said: The virgin shall be appointed as his wife. Even if she is between her parents."
"16230","(14230) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Khams, on the authority of Ibn Buraida, who said: A young woman came to Aisha. She said: My father married me to my brother’s son to relieve me of her meanness, and I hated that. So Aisha said to her: Wait until the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, comes. When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came, he sent to My father refused, so he handed the matter over to her, and she said: If the matter is up to me, then I will accept what my father did. I only wanted to know whether Is there anything wrong with women? (Ahmad 6/136 Daraqutni 45)"
"16231","(14231) Sufyan bin Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri: On the authority of Sa’id, through whom the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was informed: The orphan is in control of herself and her silence is her confession. (Abdul Razzaq 10295)"
"16232","(14232) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Amr, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger said: God, may God bless him and grant him peace: The orphan is to be kept in charge of herself, and if she accepts then it is her permission, and if she refuses then there is no permission. Aliyah

(Abu Dawud 2086; Ahmad 2/259)"
"16233","(14233) Salam narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Burda, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Either An orphan woman has been engaged and she must not be married until she is appointed as a consort. If she acknowledges, then she may be married with her acknowledgment remaining silent, and if she denies Do not marry her. (Ahmad 4/408. Daraqutni 77)"
"16234","(16234) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Omar said: The orphan woman is to be kept in charge of herself, by her consent. To be silent"
"16235","(14235) Fudayl bin Iyad narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Umar, like him."
"16236","(14236) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Ali, Omar, and Shuraih, who said: It is to be conspired. The orphan in her own right, and her consent is for her to remain silent."
"16237","(16237) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Ash-Sha’bi, on the authority of Ali that he used to say: If an orphan is married off, then If she remains silent, it is her consent, and if she does not like it, she will not be married."
"16238","(16238) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Shurayh, who said: If you remain silent and satisfied, then you have delivered. She disliked it and was reluctant to marry her."
"16239","(16239) Hushaym and Jarir both narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Abraham, regarding the orphan woman, when she is married off. He said: If she remains silent, or weeps, then it is her consent, and if she dislikes it, she will not be married, and no one will mention that she disliked it. (Ahmad 4/394, Ibn Hibban 4085)"
"16240","(14240) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Khalid bin Dinar, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: I heard him say about An orphan: If she is married off and she laughs, or cries, or remains silent, then this is her consent."
"16241","(16241) Yahya bin Adam told us, he said: Yunus bin Abi Ishaq told us, he said: Abu Burda told us, he said: Abu Moses: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The orphan is to be appointed as guardian of herself, and if she remains silent then she has given permission, and if She denied that she was not married."
"16242","(16242) It was narrated to us that Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Aroub, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Uqba bin Amir, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: If two guardians are married, it is for the first. (Muslim 7. Ibn Majah 2190)"
"16243","(14243) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Aroub, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Samarra:, on the authority of the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He said: If two guardians are married, then it goes to the first. (Abu Dawud 2081, Ibn Majah 2191)"
"16244","(16244) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, that a woman was given in marriage by a guardian for her, by the servants of God. And another man married her in Syria before Ubaid Allah. He said: Then the man came forward, and Ubaid Allah disputed with Ali and he decided against her. For the first after she gave birth to the other."
"16245","(16245) Jarir told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Abraham, who said: The first are servants of God."
"16246","(16246) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham and Ash’ath, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Shurayh, who said: If The two guardians were married, so the marriage is for the first."
"16247","(16247) Zayd bin Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Harun bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Shurayh regarding the two guardians. They get married. He said: He had the choice."
"16248","(16248) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: If two compatible people are married, it is for the first one."
"16249","(16249) Zaid bin Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Thabit bin Qais Al-Ghifari, who said: I wrote to Omar bin Abdul Aziz regarding A female servant from Jehanna was married off by her guardian to a man from Qais, and her brother married her to a man from Jehanna. So Omar bin Abdul Aziz introduced just witnesses to her and then gave her a choice, so whichever she chose was his husband."
"16250","(14250) Zayd bin Hubab told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, about two brothers who married a sister in marriage to them, and he said, “It is an option.”"
"16251","(16251) Zayd ibn Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad ibn Salamah, on the authority of Hammad regarding the two guardians, when they were married off, he said which of them She is satisfied, so he is her husband."
"16252","(16252) Mu’tamir narrated to us on the authority of Sulaiman, on the authority of Salam bin Abi Dhayyal, who said: Omar bin Abdul Aziz wrote about the two orphans: If They got married when they were young, but it was a choice."
"16253","(14253) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: She has the choice."
"16254","(16254) Al-Dahhak ibn Mukhlid narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: He has the option."
"16255","(16255) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Zam’i, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, who said: Concerning the two minor ones, he said: By choice when they are young."
"16256","(16256) Abbad bin Awwam told us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of his leaders regarding the guardian of an orphan, when he married her off while she was young. He said: Marriage is permissible, and she has the choice."
"16257","(16257) Abbad told us, on the authority of Abu Hanifa, on the authority of Hammad, who said: Marriage is permissible and she has no choice."
"16258","(14258) Ibn Idris narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Ziyad bin Alaqi, who said: A gentleman from Banu Laith proposed marriage to a man. Thayba, so her parents refused to marry her off, so she wrote to Uthman, and Uthman wrote: If he is suitable, then tell her father that He will marry her off, but if her parents refuse, then marry her off."
"16259","(14259) Saul bin Yusuf narrated to us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If the guardian and the wife disagree, the Sultan will consider it. If the guardian was ill-tempered, he would marry her off, otherwise her matter would be returned to her guardian."
"16260","(16260) Issa bin Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Sulaiman al-Taymi, on the authority of Abu Ja`far al-Ashja’i, that a woman came to Shuraih. Her mother and her uncle were with her. The mother wanted a man and the uncle wanted a man, so Shurayh gave her a choice, so she chose the one her mother chose. So Shurayh said to the uncle: Do you call for prayer? He said: No, by God, I do not give permission. He said: Will you give permission before you do not have permission? He said: No, by God, I do not permit. Shurayh said: Go and marry your daughter to whomever you wish."
"16261","(16261) Ibn Ayyash narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar, on the authority of the one who narrated to him, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Peace and blessings of God be upon him: If a man marries his son while he is unwilling, then it is not a marriage, but if he marries him while he is young, then his marriage is permissible."
"16262","(16262) Mutarrif narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hikam, on the authority of Shurayh, who said: If a man marries his son or daughter, then the choice is theirs. Sheba"
"16263","(14263) Abdullah bin Mubarak told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, Al-Hasan and his followers, they said: If he marries children Their fathers permitted their marriage."
"16264","(16244) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If a man marries his son while he is young, then his marriage is permissible. Ali, and friendship is due to the son."
"16265","(16265) A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amer, who said: No one is forced to marry except the father."
"16266","(16246) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’, who said: If a man marries his son while he He is young, so marriage is permissible and there is no divorce."
"16267","(16267) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Al-Hakam, who said: Shurayh said: If a man marries his son while he It is permissible for him to be a child, and if he reaches puberty, then if he divorces, then half the dowry is on the one who takes care of it."
"16268","(16268) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The dowry is due on the son."
"16269","(16269) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, he said: I asked Al-Hakam and Hammad about a man who marries his son while he is young. He said The ruling: It is against the son, and Hammad said: It is against the father, and his leaders said: Ibn Umar said: It is against the one you married, meaning: Friendship on the son."
"16270","(14270) Humayd narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Al-Sha’abi, who said: He is upon the father."
"16271","(16271) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Awf, on the authority of Anas, who said: Whenever he married a woman from one of his daughters, or a woman from one of his Her family said to her husband: I will marry you off if you keep her with kindness, or let her go with kindness."
"16272","(16272) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Thabit that when Ibn Abbas married He stipulated: {to keep him with kindness, or to release him with kindness}."
"16273","(16273) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Ibn Abi Maliki, that when Ibn Umar got married, he would say: I will marry you based on what God said: {Containing you with kindness, or letting go with kindness}"
"16274","(16274) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ajlan, who said: Sulayman informed me that he proposed to Ibn Umar as a master. He said to him like that."
"16275","(16275) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: I asked him, and I said: They used to stipulate the marriage contract. Marriage: {Containing oneself with kindness, or letting oneself go with kindness}? He said, so he said: That is for them, and if they did not stipulate what our companions used to stipulate."
"16276","(16276) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Juwaybir, on the authority of Ad-Dahhak {And they took from you a solemn covenant} He said: {Continuing a fair, Or a benevolent discharge}"
"16277","(16277) Issa bin Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir: {And they took from you a covenant Thick} He said: {to hold on with kindness, or to let go with kindness}"
"16278","(16278) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of Mujahid: {And they took from you a solemn covenant} He said: A contract Marriage, he said: His saying: She has been married."
"16279","(16279) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Ikrimah, and Mujahid: {And they took from you a covenant “Thick” He said: You took their women with God’s trust, and you made their private parts lawful with God’s word."
"16280","(16280) Yahya bin Yaman told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Ibn Abbas: {And they took from you a covenant Thick} He said: {to hold on with kindness, or to let go with kindness}"
"16281","(16281) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: He did not see any harm in a man marrying his female slave to him. Without any dowry or evidence."
"16282","(16282) Abd al-Rahman bin Muhammad al-Muharbi narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’, about a man who gives his male slave in marriage to his female slaves. Without witnesses, he said: It is more beloved to me to bear witness, but if he does not do so, then it is permissible."
"16283","(16283) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: They used to force the slaves to marry. And they close the door on them."
"16284","(16284) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: There is no harm in him getting married. A man gives his slave woman to death without dowry."
"16285","(14285) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Fatima, who said: I asked Ibn Sirin, he said: I said: A man said to his Mamluks: Without you, this is so-and-so’s slave girl. If you would like to take her for yourself, otherwise sell her and return her price to me. He said: Cover her with a dress."
"16286","(16286) Hatim bin Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of his father, that Ali used to say: A slave above Two"
"16287","(16287) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of a Mujahid regarding a slave who said: He marries four, and he said Atta: two."
"16288","(16288) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: A slave does not marry except two women."
"16289","(16289) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: He may marry two women."
"16290","(16290) Al-Thaqafi narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Muhammad regarding the owned man: It is disliked for him to gather more than Two, and he does not mention any female slaves or free women, but his property is the property of his master."
"16291","(16291) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: He marries two women."
"16292","(16292) Yahya bin Abdul-Malik bin Abi Ghaniyy told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Hakam, he said: If a man gives permission For his servant, in the case of a slave girl he buys, to have intercourse with her, this is marriage with the master, and he should not have intercourse with more than two."
"16293","(16293) Ibn Abi Zaydah told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: Omar said: Who knows what is permissible for the slaves? Who are the women? A man said: I. He said: How much? He said: Two women, but she remained silent."
"16294","(16294) Zayd bin Hubab told us, on the authority of Ibn Layya, on the authority of Khalid bin Abi Imran, who said: I asked Salim and Al-Qasim, about The slave, how many times should he marry? They said: Four."
"16295","(16295) Al-Muharbibi narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Al-Hikam. He said: The companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, were unanimously agreed that A slave cannot have more than two women."
"16296","(16296) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The slave above Two"
"16297","(16297) Waki` ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of al-Hasan and Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim. They said: If he marries A slave without the permission of his master, then his master gives permission, so it is permissible."
"16298","(14298) Abu Dawud told us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If the master permits it, then it is permissible."
"16299","(16299) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab, and Al-Hasan in the servant He marries without his master’s permission. They said: If he wishes, his master may permit the marriage, but if he wishes he may reject it."
"16300","(16300) Abu Dawud narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Al-Hikam. He said: He said: If the master permits it, then it is permissible, and Hammad said: He will resume. Sexual intercourse"
"16301","(16301) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If a man divorces his wife and then a slave marries her So his master then consummated the marriage with her. Al-Hasan said: He is not a husband."
"16302","(16302) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Salem, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, similar to what Al-Hasan said, and Al-Hakam said: He is a husband and he has To review it."
"16303","(16303) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’ in a woman who divorced three times and a slave married her. Without the permission of his master, he said: Ata’ said: Every marriage that is not valid in marriage means that she should not go back to her first husband."
"16304","(16304) Ismail bin Ayash told us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: No. She will go back to her, because it is a marriage that is not adulthood."
"16305","(16305) Abd al-Samad bin Abd al-Warith narrated to us, on the authority of Jarir, on the authority of Hammad, who said: It is not permissible for her to take him back to her husband. The first is until she is married to Muslims, which is permissible."
"16306","(16306) Affan narrated to us, he said: Saeed bin Zaid narrated to us, he said: Layth narrated to us, on the authority of Tawoos, who said: Every marriage was without Sunnah: A woman is not permissible for her first husband."
"16307","(16307) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, regarding the slave and the eunuch, he said: He is a husband."
"16308","(16308) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, in Al-Hurr, he married a slave woman. He said: He did not slip away. Concerning adultery, except a little, due to His saying: {And that you be patient - that is better for you}. He said: He is saying, Concerning marrying mothers."
"16309","(16309) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of the common people, on the authority of the one who narrated to him, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: He did not shun adultery except a little."
"16310","(16310) Ismail Ibn Aliyya told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he used to hate marrying mothers as much as possible. He is free unless he fears impotence."
"16311","(16311) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, who said: Ata’ asked Jabir about marrying mothers, and he said: It is not valid today."
"16312","(16312) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Burd, on the authority of Makhoul, who said: It is not appropriate for a free man to marry a motherless woman unless he does not find Long"
"16313","(16313) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, on the authority of Ammar bin Hayyan, that a woman came to Jabir bin Zayd and said: A man is proposing to my female slave. He said: Do not marry him. She said: For he fears for himself. He said: Do not marry him. She said: Because he was afraid that he would commit adultery with her, he said: So marry her."
"16314","(16314) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam and Hammad. They were asked about marrying mothers, and they said: {For him who fears Cursed on your part."
"16315","(16315) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: It is from what has been enlarged for this nation. Marriage of mothers and Christians"
"16316","(16316) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, he said: Omar said: Which of them is Abd? Whoever marries a free woman, half of him has been emancipated, and whoever is free has married a slave woman, half of him has been emancipated."
"16317","(16317) Al-Fadl narrated to us, on the authority of a partner, on the authority of Khasif, on the authority of Amir, who said: Marrying a slave woman is like a dead body, blood, and flesh. Pig is not permissible except for one who is in dire need."
"16318","(16318) Abdul Salam bin Harb told us, on the authority of Ata’ and Khasif, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: No. A free man marries any female slave except one."
"16319","(16319) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abu Hashim, on the authority of Al-Harith, who said: He said: A free man marries four female slaves. Hammad said: Two."
"16320","(16320) Ruh bin Ubadah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: A free man marries four female slaves and four Christian women, and so is the servant."
"16321","(16321) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his followers, who said: God has only made one lawful for the one who fears hardship for himself. And it did not last long."
"16322","(16322) Abu Dawud al-Talisi narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham al-Dastawai, on the authority of a man, on the authority of al-Hasan, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, forbade a free mother to be married to a free woman. (Abdul Razzaq 13099. Tabarani 17)"
"16323","(16323) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: He should not marry a free woman to a slave woman, for if he did that, he would not He is left behind."
"16324","(16324) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Burd, on the authority of Makhoul, who said: A free woman should not marry an illiterate man; The free one is upon the mother."
"16325","(16325) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Al-Minhal, on the authority of Zirr or Abbād bin Abdullah, on the authority of Ali He said: A slave woman is not married to a free woman, and a free woman is not married to a woman."
"16326","(16326) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Ash-Sha’bi, on the authority of Masruq, who said: No slave woman can marry a free woman except slaves."
"16327","(16327) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: Except the slaves."
"16328","(16328) Abdī narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, on the authority of Ibn al-Musayyab, who said: A free woman may be married to a slave woman, but no He marries a free woman."
"16329","(16329) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’ regarding a man who marries a free woman over a slave woman. He said: Good."
"16330","(16330) Abu Dawud al-Talisi narrated to us, on the authority of Zam’i, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, who said: I said to my father: A man who had sex with a free mother. And he claims that it was forbidden to him? He said: They spoke the truth."
"16331","(16331) Abdī bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id bin al-Musayyab, and the good thing about a man is that he marries The mother over the free woman. They said: He should separate him from the mother."
"16332","(16332) Hakam al-Razi told us, on the authority of Muthanna, on the authority of al-Zuhri, about a man who married a free mother. He said: His back hurts. And it is removed from him."
"16333","(16333) Abu Bakr bin Ayash told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If a free man marries a slave woman, he will be separated. Between him and her, unless she has a son from him."
"16334","(16334) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: The marriage of a free woman to a female slave is the same as the divorce of a female slave."
"16335","(16335) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Masruq, similar to it, except that he said: Like the dead, he is forced to die, so if God has made you rich, then seek help from him."
"16336","(16336) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Ash-Sha’bi, on the authority of Masruq, who said: The marriage of a free woman to a female slave is the same as the divorce of a female slave."
"16337","(16337) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Jabir bin Zaid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: If he marries If a free woman is married to a female slave, it is a divorce for a slave woman."
"16338","(16338) Abd al-Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Ibn al-Musayyab, and the good thing about a man is that he marries The Mamluks refer to Judaism and Christianity. They said: There is a difference between him and the Mamluks."
"16339","(16339) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Zuhri, regarding a man who is under a woman’s vagina. Christian: He should not marry a Muslim mother."
"16340","(16340) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, saying: A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: A Jewish woman and a Christian woman cannot marry a Muslim woman, meaning a Muslim woman."
"16341","(16341) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Manhal, on the authority of Zirr, on the authority of Ali, who said: If a free man marries The mother is an oath for the same day and for the same two days."
"16342","(16342) Ali bin Hashim told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Al-Manhal, on the authority of Zur, on the authority of Ali, who said: If he marries A free woman is assigned one day to a free woman, and two days to a free woman."
"16343","(16343) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibrahim, like him."
"16344","(16344) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, who said: The free woman has two days. And two nights, and for the mother a day and a night."
"16345","(14345) Asbat bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Ash-Sha’bi, on the authority of Masruq, who said: If they come together, divide the two-thirds of the free money. Of himself and his money."
"16346","(16346) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, on the authority of Firas, on the authority of Amir, who said: A free man marries a female slave. He divides one day and two days."
"16347","(16347) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If a free woman is married over a slave woman, the free woman is preferred, in terms of the oath. The free woman has two nights and the mother has one night."
"16348","(16348) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If he had intercourse with a slave woman and then found something to marry The freed woman, if he wishes, can take her and divide her for two nights and a night."
"16349","(16349) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’, who said: He divides two days for a free woman and one day for a female slave."
"16350","(16350) Yahya bin Ali al-Taymi told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: For the free woman there are two days and for the mother. One day"
"16351","(16351) Yunus bin Muhammad narrated to us, saying: A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: The free woman has two days. And for the mother there is a day."
"16352","(16352) Abdī bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Ibn al-Musayyab, and al-Hasan, regarding someone who marries Judaism and Christianity over the Muslim woman. They said: He divides between them equally."
"16353","(16353) Maan told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: I divided them equally."
"16354","(16354) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Ubaidah, on the authority of Abraham, who said, “He swears an oath to her just as he swears an oath to a free woman.”"
"16355","(16355) Asbat bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of al-Sha`bi, regarding a man who marries a Muslim woman and a Jewish woman, or The Christian said: He will be equal between them in the division of his wealth and his soul."
"16356","(16356) Abu Khaled told us, not by Al-Ahmar, on the authority of Sa’id, who said: I asked Al-Hakam and Hammad about it, and they said: What is in the portion? Either way"
"16357","(16357) Hushaym narrated to us, saying: Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he said: Concerning the truthfulness of a secret: if it is revealed more than it is It is taken secret and publicity is invalid."
"16358","(16358) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Shuraih, who said: It is taken secretly and is invalid. Publicity"
"16359","(16359) Mu`tamar narrated to us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: The matter is secret."
"16360","(16360) Ibn Aliya told us, on the authority of Mansour, who said: I asked Al-Hakam bin Utaiba about the man who gave a thousand in charity secretly and announced it. Alvin said: The secret is taken into account because it is the truth, and the public is invalid."
"16361","(16361) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Aoun, on the authority of Shurayh, who said: The first of the two is to be taken."
"16362","(16362) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: It is taken into account that it is open."
"16363","(16363) Ibn Mushir and Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Sha’abi, who said: It is taken into account that it is open."
"16364","(16364) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Mansour bin Abdul Rahman, who said: I met Al-Sha’bi and asked him about that, and he said, he said, : Shurayh, publicity destroys secret."
"16365","(16365) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Zayd, on the authority of Shuaib, on the authority of Abu Qalabi, who said: It is taken into account in public."
"16366","(16366) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim and Al-Shu’bi, who said: If the slave woman was under the heat, then he bought her. They said: Marriage is not permissible, and she can be his slave so he can have intercourse with her if he wants??"
"16367","(16367) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who has a slave girl under him, then he buys her, saying: He removed the bond that tied her knot."
"16368","(16368) Waki` ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, on the authority of Ali ibn Mubarak, on the authority of Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, on the authority of an alcoholic person about a man. He marries the mother and then buys her. He said: He has intercourse with her with the property."
"16369","(16369) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawoos, who said: He had intercourse with her with a king."
"16370","(16370) Hammad bin Khalid told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, who said: I asked Ata’ about a man who is under the condition of a woman. So he bought it and said: This is his female slave and he can do with it whatever he wants. He said: I asked Al-Zuhri, and he said the same thing."
"16371","(16371) Khaled bin Hayyan told us, on the authority of Ja’far bin Burqan, who said: I asked Al-Zuhri about a man who had a mother under him. So he bought it. He said: The purchase nullifies the marriage. Ja`far said: I asked Maymun bin Mihran about that, and he said: It is permissible for him in two cases. By marriage and by purchase."
"16372","(16372) Zayd ibn Harun told us, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Amr, who said: Jabir ibn Zayd was asked about a man who was He had a female slave, so he divorced her once, then he freed a slave and bought his wife. What is her status? He said: If he buys it, it will be in its secret place, and Ikrimah and Al-Hasan bin Abi Al-Hasan have issued fatwas to that effect."
"16373","(14373) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of the one who told him, on the authority of Uthman bin Affan and Zayd bin Thabit. They both said: She is not lawful for him until she marries another husband."
"16374","(16374) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, who said: I read the letter of Omar bin Abdul-Aziz: It is not permissible for him. Until she marries another husband."
"16375","(16375) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, who said: She is not permissible for him until she marries a husband. Change it"
"16376","(16376) Abu Muawiyah and Ibn Fudail told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Ad-Duha, on the authority of Masruq, who said: It is not permissible for him even She marries another husband."
"16377","(16377) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Abu Aoun, on the authority of Abu Salih al-Hanafi, on the authority of Ali, who said no. He has intercourse with her."
"16378","(16378) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Abraham, who said: She is not permissible for him until she marries a husband other than him."
"16379","(16379) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Abu Al-Duha and Al-Shu’bi, who said: It is not permissible for him except where it was forbidden to him. Until he married another husband and had intercourse with her."
"16380","(16380) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: It is not permissible for him except where it was forbidden to him."
"16381","(16381) Abbad told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: She is not permissible for him until she marries a husband. Change it"
"16382","(16382) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: She is not permissible for him until she marries another husband."
"16383","(16383) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Al-Zuhri; That Abu Abd al-Rahman asked Zayd bin Thabit about a property that was under a man and he divorced her, so they spent the night together and then bought her? He said: It is not permissible for him except in the sense in which it was forbidden to him."
"16384","(16384) Ibn Idris narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: It is not permissible for him except where it was forbidden to him."
"16385","(16385) Zayd ibn Harun told us, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Jabir ibn Zayd, who said: She is not permissible for him until she is married. A different husband"
"16386","(16386) Gandar told us, on the authority of his people, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Abraham, who said: I asked his servants about him, but he refused. Ali"
"16387","(16387) Ibn Idris narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawus, who said: He is what his right hand possesses."
"16388","(16388) Abbad bin Awwam told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: He treads on it with the right hand."
"16389","(16389) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Muhammad, on the authority of Hamid bin Abdul-Rahman, who said: Its verses are permissible. Other verses have forbidden it, and I do not command you nor forbid you."
"16390","(16390) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his followers, on the authority of Sa’id bin al-Musayyab, who said: He does not have the right to cheat on her. By the right, and if he wished, he could free her and marry her, and she was with him alone, and his commander would take her."
"16391","(16391) Abdul-A’la told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his followers, on the authority of Jabir and Abu Salamah, the same."
"16392","(16392) Abd al-Aziz ibn Abd al-Samad al-Ammi told us, on the authority of Ata’ ibn al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Ibrahim, that Ibn Masoud said: In A man, meaning a slave, who divorced his wife twice while she was a slave, and they were freed. Ibn Masoud said: He should not marry her. Until she marries another husband."
"16393","(16393) Abd al-Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of al-Hasan and Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim in The female slave is under the slave, so he divorces her twice, and they are both freed. They said: She is not lawful for him until she marries a husband. Change it"
"16394","(16394) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Amer regarding a slave who divorces a slave woman two times and they are both freed. He said: She is not permissible for him until she marries another husband."
"16395","(16395) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id ibn Abi Arouba, on the authority of the one who narrated to him, on the authority of Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, On the authority of Abu Al-Hasan, a client of Banu Nawfal, he said: My wife and I were slaves, so I divorced her twice, then We were freed after that, and she wanted to take her back, so she asked Ibn Abbas, and he said: If you take her back, then you have her as one. She went on. Two, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, decided that."
"16396","(16396) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, saying: Shayban narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Omar bin Mu’tab. On the authority of Abu Al-Hasan, a client of Banu Nawfal, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, with a similar example. 

(Abu Dawud 2181, Ahmad 1/229)"
"16397","(16397) Abdul-Wahhab bin Ata’ told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Abu Salama and Jabir bin Abdullah, who said: If She was freed during her waiting period, so he can marry her if he wants and she will be one with him."
"16398","(16398) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who married a mother between two men and bought the share of one of them. He said: He should refrain from taking care of her until he buys a share. The other"
"16399","(16399) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of a companion of his, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, the same."
"16400","(16400) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of his commanders, who said: His kingdom did not increase him except in proximity."
"16401","(16401) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, that he used to say: If a man buys a share from his wife He will not approach it until he has cleansed it."
"16402","(16402) Hushaym bin Bashir told us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Suhayb, on the authority of Anas: That the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him May He grant the emancipation of Safiyya her friendship. (Bukhari 371, Abu Dawud 2991)"
"16403","(16403) Hatim bin Ismail told us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of his father, who said: Ali said: If the man wishes, he can free the mother of his children and make He set her free."
"16404","(16404) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, he said: Saeed bin Al-Musayyab said: Whoever frees his daughter, or The mother of his son and he made freeing her a dowry, I thought that was permissible for him."
"16405","(16405) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri, that he used to say: If a man frees his female slave and makes her free, Friendship, this is permissible for him."
"16406","(16406) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Ibn Umar, about a man who frees a female slave and makes her freed. Sadaqa said: He is like a rider on his body."
"16407","(16407) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu al-Kanood, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: Like the one who He frees his female slave and marries her like a man riding his own camel."
"16408","(16408) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Ibn Sirin that he used to say, “When he makes the freeing of his female slave his ransom, it will be He likes to do something for her with that."
"16409","(16409) Abbad bin Awwam told us, on the authority of Abdul-Malik, on the authority of Ata’, about a man who said to his female slave: I have freed you and married you. He said: She is a free woman. If she wants, she can marry him, and if she wants, she can not marry him."
"16410","(16410) Abd al-A’la narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Anas bin Malik and Sa’id bin al-Musayyab that they said: If he frees her for the sake of God Almighty, he will not return to her, nor does he see any harm in freeing her in order to marry her."
"16411","(16411) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of al-Nakha’i, that he disliked it if he freed them for the sake of Allah."
"16412","(16412) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, that he hated to free her, then He marries her."
"16413","(16413) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab that he was reluctant to free her. For the sake of God Almighty, then he will marry her."
"16414","(16414) Abdul-A’la told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, that Bashir ibn Ka’b recited these verses: {So walk in On her shoulders}, and he said to his maid: If you know what is on her shoulders, you will be free before the face of God. She said: For on her shoulders Her mountains, as if his face was scorched, and he desired his maid, so he began to ask about that, so among them was someone who commanded him. And among them was someone who forbade him until he met Abu al-Darda’ and mentioned that to him, so he said: Leave what confuses you for what does not confuse you. For good is in tranquility and evil is in uncertainty, so abandon that."
"16415","(16415) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his followers, that Al-Hasan and Ata did not see any harm in that, even if He freed her for the sake of God, and they say: This is greater in reward."
"16416","(16416) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that when he was asked about a man who freed his female slave, And he will marry her even if he sees no harm in that, and if he frees her for the sake of God, he will marry her."
"16417","(16417) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Al-Salt bin Bahram, on the authority of Shaqiq, who said: Hudhafi married a Jewish woman. So Omar wrote to him saying, “Let her go.” He wrote to her, “If it is forbidden, let her go.” He wrote to her, “Indeed, no.” I claim that it is forbidden, but I fear that prostitutes will use it."
"16418","(16418) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Abdul-Malik, who said: I asked Ata’ about the marriage of Jewish and Christian women. He thought about it and said: That was the case, and the things that are accepted are few."
"16419","(16419) Yahya bin Sa’id narrated to us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that he hated it. He marries the wives of the People of the Book, and sees no harm in feeding them."
"16420","(16420) Waki` ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, on the authority of Ja`far ibn Burqan, on the authority of Maimun ibn Mihran, on the authority of Ibn Umar that he hated it. Marrying the wives of the People of the Book, and he recited: {And do not marry polytheists until they believe}"
"16421","(16421) Waki` ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Hubayra, on the authority of Ali, who said: He got married A man from the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he is Jewish."
"16422","(16422) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Hubayra that Talhahi married a Christian woman."
"16423","(16423) Muhammad bin Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, who said: We witnessed Al-Qadisiyyah with Sa’d. At that time, we did not find a way to marry Muslim women, so we married Jewish women and Christian women. Some of us divorced, and some of us kept them away."
"16424","(16424) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of a neighbor of Hudhayfah, on the authority of Hudhayfah that he had intercourse with She is Jewish and she has two Arab women."
"16425","(16425) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: There is no harm in marrying a Christian woman."
"16426","(16426) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Ash-Sha’bi, that he saw no harm in marrying among the People of the Book."
"16427","(16427) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Abu Iyad, who said: There is no harm in marrying Jewish women. And Christian women, except those who are warlike."
"16428","(16428) Abdī narrated to us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Ibn al-Musayyab and al-Hasan. They said: There is no harm for a man to marry Four of the People of the Book."
"16429","(16429) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Abu al-Rabi`, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: There is no harm in a man having intercourse. Four of the People of the Book."
"16430","(14430) Ruh bin Ubadah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: A free man marries four female slaves and four Christian women and the servant as well."
"16431","(14431) Abbad bin Awwam told us, on the authority of Sufyan bin Hussein, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: No. It is permissible to marry the wives of the People of the Book if they are at war. Al-Hakam said: So I told it to Abraham, and he liked it."
"16432","(16432) Abd al-Rahman bin Muhammad al-Muharbi narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of al-Hakam, on the authority of Abu Iyad, who said: The women of the People of the Book For us it is lawful, except for those of war, for their wives and their slaughtered animals are forbidden to you."
"16433","(14433) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Ghaniyya, on the authority of Al-Hikam. He said: Among the People of the Book are those who do not It is permissible for us to marry him or to slaughter him, people of war."
"16434","(14434) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, who said: Abu Bakr bin Abdullah told me, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr. Al-Awari, and Yahya bin Abdul-Rahman bin Hatib, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Abdullah bin Utba and on the authority of Amr bin Sulaym Al-Zarqiy, on the authority of Ibn al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu al-Nadr, on the authority of Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, that they said in the mirror from the People of the Book, If she enters from the land of war, she will enter the land of the Arabs in safety. If she appears at rest in the land of the Arabs, then there is no harm in marrying her. Muslim, and if you do not reveal this except at the time of engagement, then you are not married."
"16435","(16435) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Abu Misra, who said: The imamates of the People of the Book are in the same position as their free women."
"16436","(14436) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he said: He only granted permission to these slave women regarding the wives of his family. The Book did not permit female slaves."
"16437","(14437) Uthman narrated to us, on the authority of Thawr, on the authority of Makhoul, that he disliked marrying the People of the Book."
"16438","(14438) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid: {of your believing girls}, he said: A free Muslim should not marry a mother from the People of the Book."
"16439","(14439) Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman narrated to us on the authority of Miswar that Omar bin Abdul Aziz wrote: If a man enters a woman, it is obligatory The immediate and the later, unless you stipulate the later."
"16440","(16440) A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, regarding a man who marries a woman until he can afford it. He said: It was He says: To death, or separation."
"16441","(16441) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he used to say regarding the fixed period of dowry: It is permissible, unless It will have a known term."
"16442","(14442) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Shuraih, who said: A man married a woman on a fixed basis. And he came to Misra and brought it to Shurayh. He said, “Show us a Misra and we will take it for you.”"
"16443","(14443) Azhar al-Samman told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Iyas ibn Muawiyah, who said: If he enters it, there is no claim for it. The term"
"16444","(14444) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, who said: The urgent means death or separation."
"16445","(14445) Abu Dawud narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, who said: I heard Hammad saying: It is available, you can take it if you wish."
"16446","(16446) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Burd, on the authority of Makhoul and al-Zuhri, who said: Concerning a man who married a woman and had intercourse with her. So he saw in her madness, or leprosy, or leprosy, or impotence, that she would be restored from this, and she would have the dowry that made her immediate relief possible. And the future, and His friendship is upon him who deceives him."
"16447","(16447) Abduh bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Ali, that he used to hate him. Christian sacrifices of Banu Taghlib and their wives, and he says: They are Arabs."
"16448","(16448) Abduh told us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Al-Hasan that he did not see any harm in that and he said: They committed suicide. religion, that is their religion."
"16449","(14449) Zayd ibn Harun told us, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Amr ibn Harim, who said: Jabir ibn Zayd was asked about Christians. The Arabs: Are their wives permissible for the Muslims? He said: They are not among the People of the Book, and neither their wives nor their food are permissible for the Muslims."
"16450","(16450) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Imran bin Hudayr, he said: Ikrimah said: {And whoever of you befriends them is one of them} He said: Arab Christians in their sacrifices and in their women."
"16451","(14451) Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: Eat Sacrifice the Banu Tha'labiyah and marry their wives, for God Almighty says: {O you who have believed, do not take Jews as Jews. And the Christians are allies of one another, allies of one another.} If they had not been of them except through guardianship, they would have been of them."
"16452","(16452) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Mu’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Ali, that he hated Sacrifices of Arab Christians and their women."
"16453","(14453) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim, that he hated it."
"16454","(14454) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Al-Hasan. He said: There is no harm in him."
"16455","(14455) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Abdul Hamid, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Simak bin Salamah that Shurayh permitted the marriage of a guardian guardian"
"16456","(16456) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Al-Harith, who said: The guardian consults the executor regarding marriage and the one who performs the marriage contract. The guardian"
"16457","(14457) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Hammad, regarding a guardian who married off an orphan girl who was young in his custody. He said: It is permissible."
"16458","(14458) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning the guardian getting married, he said: It is permissible."
"16459","(14459) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Harith, on the authority of Ash-Shu’bi, on the authority of Al-Hakam and Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim. They said: What did the executor do? It is permissible except for marriage."
"16460","(16460) Saul bin Yusuf narrated to us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan that he did not assign anything to the heir regarding the matter of marriage except That he said: You are my guardian in the marriage of my sisters and my daughters. If he did so, then the guardian has more right than the guardian. Otherwise, the guardian has more right than the guardian. The guardian"
"16461","(16461) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, about a woman who married a man who was free and found a slave. He said: He made a choice."
"16462","(14462) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he was asked about a man who deluded himself with a woman and claimed that he was free. Abd said: He chose."
"16463","(16463) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, about a woman who was deceived by a slave and was You think he is free. Ibn Shihab said: He was given the choice."
"16464","(16464) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Amr, who said: Jabir bin Zaid was asked about a servant who went to a people. So he told them that he was free, so they married him as a free woman, then they learned after that that he was a slave by whom she had been deceived. He said: If she knew about him If she wants, she can stay with him, and if she wants, she can leave him, and he has no right over her."
"16465","(16465) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khalid, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: Any slave who comes to a free man So she married him, and after that she learned that he was a slave, so if she wanted, she could stay with him, and if she wanted, she could leave him."
"16466","(16466) Waki` ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, who said: If the son marries, it is not permissible for the father to enter With her, or he does not consummate her, and if the father marries and it is not permissible for the son, he may consummate her with her, or he does not consummate with her."
"16467","(16467) Hatim bin Wardan narrated to us, on the authority of Burd, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: Whoever owns the marriage contract of a woman, it has been forbidden to his son. The same applies to his father and to whomever he stripped and looked at the private parts."
"16468","(16468) Issa bin Yunus told us on the authority of Abu Bakr, on the authority of Makhoul, who said: Which of the two of them owns the marriage of a woman who is forbidden to the other?"
"16469","(14469) Abu Dawud narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hurri, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who married a woman and divorced her before consummating the sexual intercourse with her. Did his father marry her? He thought about it, and God Almighty said: {And the relatives of your children}"
"16470","(14470) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan and Muhammad. They said: Three ambiguous verses: {And the wives of your sons} and {What Your fathers married} and {and your mothers} He said: Ash'ath: And this fourth is not ambiguous {and your stepsons who are in Your wives are among your wives.} So Muadh recited it until the end."
"16471","(16471) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Ubaidah, on the authority of Abraham, who said: If a man marries a woman and does not have sexual intercourse with her, he does not have sexual intercourse with her. Permissible for his father"
"16472","(16472) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Makhoul, that Omar stripped his two female slaves, and one of them asked him about them. He built it and said: It is not permissible for you."
"16473","(14473) Abdullah bin Mubarak narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Makhoul, that Omar stripped two of his female slaves, and some of them sought them out. He built it and said: It is not permissible for you."
"16474","(14474) Abdullah bin Numir told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather that he stripped Then one of his children asked her about her, and he said: It is not permissible for you."
"16475","(14475) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar, Sulaiman bin Hayyan, narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Muhammad, on the authority of Abdullah bin Aamer said that when death approached his father, he forbade his sons and his neighbor from having sexual intercourse with her. Some of them said: We do not know whether he had intercourse with her unless he was informed of a matter from her that he disliked for his son to know about it."
"16476","(16476) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Makhoul, that Omar stripped his slave girl, looked at her, and asked him: Some of his children gave it to her, and he said: It is not permissible for you."
"16477","(14477) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, something like this."
"16478","(14478) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hakam, he said: Masruq said when he attended his death: I was not afflicted by This is my maid, except what is forbidden to my children by touching and seeing."
"16479","(16479) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, Mujahid said: If a man touches the private parts of a mother, or touches her private parts So he comforted her, or had intercourse with her, for that would make her sacred to his father and to his son."
"16480","(16480) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he asked about a man who stripped his female slave, whether it was permissible for his son, or For his father, he hated it if he kissed her, or stripped her for lust."
"16481","(16481) Al-Thaqafi narrated to us, on the authority of Muthanna, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of Ibn Omar, who said: Whatever man is stripped A female slave, and if he looks at that matter from her, then she is not permissible for his son."
"16482","(16482) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, that he asked Al-Sha’bi about him, and he said: They claimed that a man bought A slave girl, and his wife was afraid that he would take her, so she ordered a son of hers, a boy, to lie on her to make her sacred to her. Her husband"
"16483","(14483) Hammad bin Khalid told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who disliked a man having intercourse with a woman before kissing her. His father, or he looked at her scenes."
"16484","(16484) Issa bin Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Bakr, on the authority of Makhoul, who said: Any man who strips his maidservant will be forbidden to me. His son and his father."
"16485","(14485) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Amr bin Haram, who said: Jabir bin Zaid was asked about his neighbor. It belonged to a man, and he touched her vagina with his hand, or looked at her private parts, and then gave her to a son of his. Would it be better for him to have intercourse with her? He said: No."
"16486","(14486) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Amr, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, who said: Masruq wrote to his family: Look. My maidservant, do not sell her, for I have not acquired anything from her except that which is forbidden to my children by touch and sight."
"16487","(16487) Ali bin Musahir narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Imran bin Al-Husayn, about a man who falls On his wife’s mother. He said: His wife is forbidden to him."
"16488","(14488) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Yahya bin Yamar, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: Two things are forbidden for her to sin, but this is not forbidden for her."
"16489","(14489) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamiya, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: No. God looks at a man who looks at the private parts of a woman and her daughter. (Daraqutni 92)"
"16490","(16490) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Hani, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: And peace be upon him: Whoever looks at a woman’s private parts, neither her mother nor her daughter is permissible for him. (Bayhaqi 170)"
"16491","(16491) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim and Amir, regarding a man who had sexual intercourse with his wife’s son, and they said: They were forbidden to him. Both of them, and Abraham said, and they used to say that if a man looks at a woman in something that is not permissible for him, or touches her For some reason, they were completely forbidden to him."
"16492","(16492) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Ata’, who said: If a man has forbidden intercourse with a woman, her daughter is forbidden to her. And if he had a son, her mother would be forbidden to her."
"16493","(16493) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Musabah, who said: I asked Abraham about a man who committed adultery with his mother and then wanted to get married. He said to her mother: He will not marry her."
"16494","(16494) Ubayd Allah told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, he said: I asked Al-Hakam and Hammad about a man who committed adultery with his wife’s mother. They said: He loves It is upon us that he separate from her."
"16495","(16495) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If a man winks at his female slave, Unfortunately, he did not marry her mother or her daughters."
"16496","(16496) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Uthman ibn Al-Aswad, on the authority of Mujahid and Ata’, who said: If a man commits adultery with a woman She is permissible for him, but none of her daughters are permissible for him."
"16497","(16497) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his leaders, who said: Jabir bin Zayd and Al-Hasan used to deny that A man touching his wife means that a man has intercourse with his wife’s mother."
"16498","(16498) Ismail Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Yazid al-Rashk, who said: I asked Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab about a man who commits immoral acts. By his wife’s mother, and he said: As for the mother, it is forbidden, and as for the daughter, it is permissible."
"16499","(16499) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubaid Allah, on the authority of his father, who said: Omar was asked about the plural of the mother. And her daughter is from the kingdom of Yemen. He said: I would not like for him to tell them all."
"16500","(16500) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Tariq, on the authority of Qais bin Abi Hazim, who said: I said to Ibn Abbas: The man has intercourse with the slave woman. And her two daughters will be two kingdoms with him, and he said: I made them forbidden by some verses and made lawful by other verses, but I was not able to do them."
"16501","(16501) Abd al-A’la ibn Abd al-A’la narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Abu al-Zinad, on the authority of Abd Allah ibn Nayyar. Al-Aslami said: I had a maid with whom I used to have intercourse, and she had a son of hers with her, so her daughter came to me and wanted to He withheld her and had intercourse with her daughter, so I said: I will not do that until I ask Uthman bin Affan. So I asked him about that, and he said: As for me, I did not Shall we emerge from them as one?"
"16502","(16502) Yahya bin Saeed narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ibn Abi Mulkiya that Muadh bin Ubaid Allah bin Muammar asked Aisha, and he said: I have a neighbor who was infected by her, and she has a son who has come to her and he has been infected by her? So she forbade him, and he said: No, even if you say, “It is forbidden.” She said: “None of my family, nor those who obey me, will do it.” She asked Ibn Omar denied me."
"16503","(16503) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Amir, who said: A man from Hamdan had a son and a daughter, so it was It falls on them, so Ali was informed of that, so he asked him, and he said: Yes, and Ali said to him: When a verse is made lawful for you and prohibited for you Other than that, their possession is the forbidden verse."
"16504","(14504) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid told us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Rafi’, on the authority of Ibn Munabbih, who said: In the Torah. Which God revealed to Moses: “No man shall uncover the private parts of a woman or her daughter except one cursed. He has not separated for us any heat or Owned"
"16505","(16505) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Al-Jariri, on the authority of Abu Nadhri, who said: A man came to Omar and said: I have a son. And her two daughters, and they both liked me. Should I please them? He said: Some verses are permissible and some are forbidden. As for me, I was not close to that."
"16506","(16506) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of Sa’id, who said: A man should not have intercourse between a woman and her daughter, nor between The woman and her sister."
"16507","(14507) Abdullah bin Mubarak told us, on the authority of Musa bin Ayyub, on the authority of his uncle, on the authority of Ali, who said: I asked him about a man who had Two sisters. He had intercourse with one of them, then wanted to have intercourse with the other. He said: No, not until he expels her from his kingdom. He said: I said: It is. Did Abdul marry her? He said: No, until he expels her from his kingdom."
"16508","(14508) Abdullah bin Idris, Waki’, narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bai, on the authority of Abu Aoun, on the authority of Abu Salih al-Hanafi, that Ibn Al-Kawa'i asked Ali about combining two sisters, and he said: I made one verse forbidden to her and made others permissible, and neither I nor I do it. Welcome"
"16509","(16509) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: They angered Ibn Masoud about the two sisters. The two kingdoms, so he became angry and said: One of you has taken possession of what his right hand possesses."
"16510","(16510) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Burd, on the authority of Makhoul, about a man who has two female sisters, and he has intercourse with one of them. He said: No. He has intercourse with the other woman until he expels her from his possession."
"16511","(16511) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Abu al-Jahm, on the authority of Abu al-Akhdar, on the authority of Ammar, who said: What God has forbidden Of the silks, he has forbidden them from the slaves, except that a man may gather as many as he wants from the slaves."
"16512","(16512) Khalid ibn Mukhlid narrated to us, on the authority of Malik ibn Anas, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Qubaisah ibn Dhu’ib, who said: He was asked Othman bin Affan, on the authority of the two sisters from the kingdom of the right, he brought them together and said: What verses from the Book of God are lawful for them A verse made it forbidden, but as for me, I do not like to do that."
"16513","(16513) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Maymun, on the authority of Ibn Umar that he was asked about a man who had two maternal sisters who had two sisters. Does it fall on one of them on the other? He said: Ibn Umar said: He does not have sexual intercourse with the other woman as long as the one with whom he had sexual intercourse remains in his possession."
"16514","(16514) Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash told us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz ibn Rafi’, who said: I asked Ibn al-Hanafiyyah about a man. He has two sister mothers, whom should he have intercourse with? He said: Both verses are lawful and both verses are forbidden. Then I came to Ibn al-Musayyab, and he said the same as what Muhammad said. Then I asked Ibn Munabbih. He said: I bear witness that, according to what God revealed to Moses, he is cursed whoever brings two sisters together. He said: He did not separate for us two free women or Mamloukateen. He said: I went back to Ibn al-Musayyab and told him, and he said: God is great."
"16515","(16515) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Mubarak, on the authority of Ibn Thuban, on the authority of Aisha, that she hated him."
"16516","(16516) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who had two female sisters, and he had intercourse with one of them, then withheld her. Is it permissible for him to have intercourse with the other? He said: It was It is amazing that he does not cheat on her until this that he cheated on is removed from his kingdom."
"16517","(16517) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam and Hammad, who said: If a man has two sisters, he should not marry one of them. From them"
"16518","(16518) Asbat bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, and Ibn Sirin, who said: It is forbidden to bring together female slaves what is forbidden. From collecting silks, except for the number."
"16519","(16519) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah, who said: A man asked Othman, on the authority of the two sisters, he joined them together and said: “What verses are lawful for you and what are forbidden for them? Neither commanded you nor forbade you.” So he met them. Ali was at the door, and he said: What did you ask him about? So he told him, and he said: But I forbid you, even if I had a way against you, then I did that. I would have hurt you"
"16520","(14520) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Asim ibn Umar, on the authority of his followers, on the authority of al-Qasim ibn Muhammad that Hayya The living Arabs asked Mu’awiyah about the two sisters that the right hand possessed, that would be with a man and he would have intercourse with them. He said: Not. That is bad. Al-Nu’man bin Bashir heard about that and said, “Have you issued a fatwa for such-and-such?” He said: “Yes.” He said: “What if it were?” Is there a man whose sister is a slave, and is it permissible for him to have intercourse with her? He said: By God, if you have rejected me, I will catch you, so tell them to avoid that, for it is not appropriate for them. He said: I said: This is the kinship of freedmen and others."
"16521","(14521) Ismail Ibn Aliyya told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Aroub, on the authority of his followers, regarding a man who marries a woman and then He divorces her before he has intercourse with her. Should he marry her mother? He said: Ali said: He is in the same position as his stepson."
"16522","(14522) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Khalas, on the authority of Ali, like him."
"16523","(14523) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Arouba, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab, on the authority of Zayd ibn It is proven that he saw nothing wrong with it if he divorced her, and he hated her if she died with him."
"16524","(14524) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Abu Bakr ibn Hafs ibn Umar ibn Sa’d that Muslim ibn Awamir bin Al-Ajda’ from Banu Bakr bin Kinanan told him that his father married him to a woman in Taif. He said: He did not I had intercourse with her until my uncle died, on her mother’s behalf, and her mother had a lot of money, so my father said to me, “Do you have anything to do with her mother?” So I said: I wanted to, but how, since she had married her daughter. He said: So I asked Ibn Abbas, and he said, Marry her. I asked Ibn Omar, and he said: No. He married her: He said: So Abu Awamir wrote about that to Muawiyah and told him in his letter what Ibn Abbas said and what Ibn Umar said, so Muawiyah wrote to him: I do not permit what God has made unlawful, nor do I make unlawful what God has made lawful, and you and that and many women. He said: He did not forbid me or give permission, and my father left her and we did not marry her."
"16525","(14525) Waki` ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Farwa, on the authority of Abu Amr al-Shaibani, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Masoud said that he issued a fatwa regarding a man who married a woman and divorced her before he consummated the marriage with her, or she died with him, and he said: There is no problem. That he should marry her mother, then he came to Medina and returned, and he came to them and comforted them, and she had given birth to children."
"16526","(16526) Ibn Aliya told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Dawud informed me, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Masruq, concerning {your mothers of wives}, he said: What God has sent, so they send, and whatever He has made clear, so follow."
"16527","(14527) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, who said: Ikrimah informed me, on the authority of Mujahid, that he said about {And the mothers of your wives and your stepchildren who are in your laps}: I mean by them both combined."
"16528","(14528) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, who said: I said to Ata’: A man marries a woman and then neither sees her nor sees her. He has intercourse with her until he divorces her. Should he marry her mother? He said: No, it is mursal."
"16529","(14529) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Burd, on the authority of Makhoul, that it was distasteful for him if a man had possession of a woman to He marries her."
"16530","(16530) Affan narrated to us, saying: Hammam narrated to us, on the authority of his followers, who said: Asim bin Sa’id al-Dhudhali informed me, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab said that Zayd ibn Thabit was reluctant to marry the daughter of a woman whose mother had died with him before he entered With it"
"16531","(16531) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, saying: I said to Ibn Abi Najih: A man marries a woman and then divorces her before he He may consummate the marriage with her. Will he marry her mother? He said: I heard Ikrimah forbade giving and giving."
"16532","(16532) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Imran bin Al-Husayn in {Ummat Your women} He said: They are ambiguous."
"16533","(16533) Abu Dawud told us, on the authority of Zam’a, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, that he disliked it, and said, “It is ambiguous.”"
"16534","(14534) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: Ambiguous"
"16535","(16535) Ismail Ibn Aliyya told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, who said: Ibn Umar used to see his servant walking around in His money, so there is no shame in that."
"16536","(16536) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, who said: Nafi’ wrote to me that the servant is being content with his wealth and is not being content with it. On her master's property."
"16537","(16537) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: He did not see any harm in a slave being pleased with his permission. Her master"
"16538","(14538) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Omar bin Abdulaziz, who said: There is no harm in The servant is pleased."
"16539","(14539) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hasan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, that he said: There is no harm in it."
"16540","(16540) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Qais bin Muslim, on the authority of Al-Sha’abi, who said: There is no harm in him."
"16541","(16541) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Ash-Shu’bi, who said: If the master gives permission to his servant to be pleased, let him take it. From them whatever he wants."
"16542","(16542) Ismail bin Ayyash narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: We did not see a slave being frivolous with his money. Her master is mighty."
"16543","(14543) Abdou bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: There is no harm in him."
"16544","(14544) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Abbas bin Abdullah bin Ma’abad, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; He had a servant who was a merchant, and he used to call him in and he would take the six and seven o’clock."
"16545","(16545) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Salama bin Kahil, on the authority of Al-Hakam, who said: He may marry but not keep a wife."
"16546","(16546) Ibn Aliya told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibn Sirin that he loved to marry her."
"16547","(16547) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’abi, he said: I asked Hammad about that, and he said: Have you not heard? But God says: {Except upon Their wives or those whom their right hands possess}"
"16548","(14548) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hakam, and Ibn Sirin that they disliked that he should be led away, even if he gave him permission. His Lord"
"16549","(16549) Abdou bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, that he hated to be conceited. The slave"
"16550","(16550) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Omar, he said: Whoever married If a woman is afflicted with leprosy, or leprosy, or madness, and he enters into her, then she is entitled to dowry for what is permissible from her private parts, and that is a fine on her. Her guardian"
"16551","(16551) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Hikam. He said: Ali used to say regarding the insane and the lepers: He enters into his wife's mouth, and if he does not enter, he separates them."
"16552","(16552) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Amr ibn Dinar, on the authority of Jabir ibn Zayd, who said: Four are not permissible in Sell or marry: the leper, the insane, the leper, and the horned woman."
"16553","(14553) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Khalid, that a man married a woman and had intercourse with her, then he found a defect in her and wrote to her. Omar bin Abdul Aziz about that, so he wrote that he had entrusted them with something greater than that, so he rewarded her for it."
"16554","(16554) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan. He was asked about a man who marries a woman and then consummates the marriage with her. There is a disease on her because it was obligatory on her."
"16555","(16555) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Amr ibn Maimun, on the authority of Amr ibn Abdul Aziz, who said: He has nothing but his trusts. In-laws"
"16556","(16556) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: A free woman is not returned from a defect."
"16557","(16557) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Ash-Shu’bi, on the authority of Shurayh that he used to compensate the lepers."
"16558","(16558) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Burd, on the authority of Makhul and al-Zuhri, who said: Concerning a man who married a woman, and he went in and saw Insanity, or leprosy, or leprosy, or impotence: She will be repelled from this, and she will have the dowry that will bring her immediate and future relief. And His friendship is with those who deceive Him."
"16559","(16559) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Jamil, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ka’b, or Ka’b bin Abdullah, who said: He got married. The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, saw a woman from Ghifar, and he sat next to her as a man sits at a mirror, and he noticed leprosy in her scratches. So he got up from her and said: Straighten your clothes and go back to your house."
"16560","(16560) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Zuhair, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: Do not reject it. Freedom from shame."
"16561","(16561) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, that he said: If a man marries a woman and there is no shame on the man, You are given the choice whether it is madness, leprosy, or leprosy."
"16562","(16562) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of the ruling that he said about a man who marries a woman and he suffers from leprosy. He said: He did not see anything in the man, and as for leprosy, if she wished, she could stay with him, and if she wished, she could leave him."
"16563","(16563) Muhammad bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Ala’, who is Ayyub, on the authority of his followers, about a man who married a woman. And he has insanity, or an incurable disease that you do not know about. He said: It is the option if you know. And Abu Hashim said: It is his wife, if he wishes. He retains him, and if he wishes, he divorces him."
"16564","(16544) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid told us, on the authority of Musa bin Abi Aisha, who said: I asked my wife about a man who buys. Or he takes a Magian slave captive and then has intercourse with her before she learns Islam. He said: It is not appropriate, and I asked Sa`id ibn Jubair, and he said: He is not better than her if he does that."
"16565","(16565) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Burd, on the authority of Makhoul, who said: If her child is a Magi, then he should not marry her. Until you are safe."
"16566","(16566) Issa bin Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Al-Zuhri. He said, I heard him say: Do not approach the Magi. Until she says there is no god but Allah, then if she says that, then it is Islam."
"16567","(16567) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Abu Salamah, in the Magi, he said: Do not approach it when Thank you"
"16568","(14568) Hatem bin Wardan told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; In the Magi, she is with the man and he says: He will not have intercourse with her."
"16569","(16569) Jarir bin Abdul Lahmid told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: When the Magi women and his slave were taken captive Idols were offered Islam and forced, so if they converted to Islam, they were accepted and used, and if they refused to submit, they were used and not accepted."
"16570","(16570) Al-Thaqafi narrated to us, on the authority of Muthanna, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, who said: There is no harm in buying. The man who is a magician's slave girl will be pleased with her."
"16571","(16571) Ubayd Allah narrated to us, on the authority of Muthanna, who said: Ata’, Tawus, and Amr ibn Dinar did not see any harm in taking things easy. The man who is a magician and Saeed bin Al-Musayyab hated him."
"16572","(16572) Shadhan narrated to us, saying: Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Bakr ibn Ma’iz, on the authority of Rabi’ ibn Khuthaym, who said : If a polytheist mother befalls you, do not come to her until she has delivered and bathed."
"16573","(16573) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: When the Jewish and Christian women were taken captive Islam was offered to them and they were forced to convert to it. If they converted to Islam or did not convert to Islam, they would settle down and be used."
"16574","(16574) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Burd, on the authority of alcohol in a man if he has a Jewish child, or Christian, for he is intercourse with her."
"16575","(16575) Hatem bin Wardan told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The Jew and the Christian walk together."
"16576","(16576) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: If a man strikes a polytheist slave girl, So let him confirm it with the testimony of there is no god but Allah. If she refuses to acknowledge it, that will not prevent him from having intercourse with her."
"16577","(16577) Abduh bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Mu’awiyah bin Qurayh, who said, “Abdullah used to hate it.” His nation is a polytheist."
"16578","(16578) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: If he has a mother from the People of the Book, then he may He covers her if he wishes and forces her to wash."
"16579","(16579) Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Najiya, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Ibn Masoud regarding the captive: He should not even have intercourse with her. May you be blessed and greeted."
"16580","(16580) Zaid narrated to us, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Amr bin Haram, who said: Jabir bin Zaid was asked about a man who buys The slave girl from captivity, and he falls on her. He said: No, until he teaches her about prayer, washing from impurity, and shaving the pubic hair."
"16581","(16581) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Qays ibn Muslim, on the authority of Al-Hasan ibn Muhammad that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him He wrote to the Magians of the people of Hijr, offering Islam to them. Whoever converted to Islam would accept it, and whoever did not submit would be beaten. The penalty is neither marrying their wives nor eating their sacrifices. (Abdul Razzaq 10028, Bayhaqi 285)"
"16582","(16582) Hushaym told us, on the authority of the common people, he said: Someone who heard Saeed bin Al-Musayyab told me that it was disliked for a man to ask The child from the mother if she was the child of adultery."
"16583","(16583) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, who said: The child of fornication is kept secret and does not seek her children."
"16584","(14584) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Uthman ibn al-Harith, on the authority of Abu al-Rawa`, he said: I asked Ibn Umar about the child of adultery. He said: There are many women."
"16585","(16585) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibrahim ibn al-Muhajir, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said, “There is no harm in seeking secrets.”"
"16586","(16586) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who has intercourse with a female slave due to his fornication. He said: It is like the display of his wealth that he has intercourse with."
"16587","(14587) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: There is no harm for a man to buy the child of an adulteress and be happy with it."
"16588","(14588) Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Sayyar, a servant of Mu’awiyah, who said: A man wanted to marry a girl. He committed adultery, and he asked a man from the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about that, and he said: No, if he marries her mother, he is more beloved to me than To marry her."
"16589","(16589) Humayd narrated to us, on the authority of Hasan, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Sirin regarding a man who indulges in the child of adultery. He said: And what His sin is what his parents did."
"16590","(16590) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Habib, who said: I heard Al-Hakam saying: If it were mine His slave-girl, the son of fornication, I did not care if he had intercourse with her."
"16591","(16591) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Abu Ma’bad; That Ibn Abbas had intercourse with a slave girl after denying her children."
"16592","(16592) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Lubab, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; He saw nothing wrong with a man having intercourse with his female slave if she was unrighteous, and he saw that as a protection for her."
"16593","(16593) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Omar, on the authority of Muhammad bin Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of his father He had intercourse with his slave girl after she had committed debauchery."
"16594","(16594) Ali bin Hashim told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, regarding a man who has intercourse with his female slave while she has committed adultery. He said: He has the option, if he wishes, to have intercourse with her, and if he wishes, he can hold her."
"16595","(16595) Abduh narrated to us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Qurayh, who said: Abd Allah hated his nation. She committed adultery"
"16596","(16596) Al-Fadl narrated to us, on the authority of Mubarak, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: I heard him and he was asked about a man who sees his nation exploding. Did he have intercourse with her? He said: No, no honor."
"16597","(16597) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If a man sees his wife She explodes, but that does not make her forbidden to her."
"16598","(16598) Abu Usama told us, he said: Jarir bin Hazim told us, on the authority of Qays bin Saad, on the authority of a giving woman who intends to commit adultery. His wife said: This does not make her forbidden to him."
"16599","(16599) Abu Dawud narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad ibn Muslim, on the authority of Imran ibn Abdullah, on the authority of Salem, a man said to him: I saw a man with my wife, and he said: You make yourself feel good, or how you make yourself feel good if you keep her, and I saw what I saw it but it was not forbidden to you."
"16600","(16600) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who finds his wife obscene and hates to touch her."
"16601","(16601) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid ibn Jabir, on the authority of Makhoul, who said: If a man sees If his wife is immoral, it is not permissible for him to hold her, and if he himself is immoral, it is not permissible for her to stay with him."
"16602","(16602) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaddad, who said: I was sitting with Ibn Abbas in Zamzam, and a man came to him and mentioned to him that he had had an abortion with his wife, so she claimed that she had committed adultery, so Ibn Abbas said to him: What a miserable thing you have done. If she did what she admitted to doing against herself, then keep your wife, and if she did not, then let her go. May God bless you"
"16603","(16603) Abdah bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Adiy bin Thabit, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: If one of you sees If his wife or the mother of his children commits an indecency, do not approach her."
"16604","(16604) Abu Dawud narrated to us, on the authority of Zam’a, on the authority of Salama bin Wharam, who said: I was sitting next to a peacock, and a man said to him: I found a man sitting with me, and a peacock said: If your soul is willing to hold her, and you have seen what I have seen, then you know best."
"16605","(16605) Zayd bin Harun told us: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ubaid bin Umair, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, said: A man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: I have a woman whom I love. He said: Divorce her. He said: I will not be patient with her. He said: So enjoy her.

(Abu Dawud 2042, Bayhaqi 155)"
"16606","(16406) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Qais bin Saad, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: He exceeded You are mahram to mahram, even if his wife is not mahram to him."
"16607","(16607) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: If a man commits adultery with his wife’s sister, she is not forbidden. Ali, he does not make forbidden what is permissible."
"16608","(16608) Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Uthman al-Batti, on the authority of Ibn Ash’u, that he was asked about it, and he said, “It is not forbidden.” What is forbidden is what is permissible, I dared to accept it, and Ibrahim and Al-Sha’biyy accepted it."
"16609","(16609) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: His wife was forbidden to him."
"16610","(16610) And Sa`id told us that his leaders said: This does not make her forbidden to him, except that he does not even cheat on his wife. The period with which it was built has expired."
"16611","(16611) Abdul-A’la told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Jabir ibn Zayd, and the good news is that they both said: It was forbidden to him. His wife"
"16612","(16612) Abd al-A’la narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of some of his companions, on the authority of al-Nakha’i: It is like the saying of Qatadah, even if it is Pregnant until she gives birth."
"16613","(16613) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of a friend of his, on the authority of Ata’, who said: This does not make her forbidden to him."
"16614","(16614) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Sa’id, that he reported to him on the authority of al-Sha’bi that he said: This does not make it forbidden for him."
"16615","(16615) Abu Abd al-Samad al-Ammi told us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Imran bin Husayn, who said: His wife was forbidden to him."
"16616","(16616) Abu Abd al-Samad al-Ammi told us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Yahya bin Yamar, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: His wife was not forbidden to him."
"16617","(16617) Abd al-Aziz ibn Abd al-Samad al-Ammi narrated to us, on the authority of Badil ibn Misra al-Uqaili, on the authority of Abu The two conditions are that a man married to a man from the Levant a daughter who had a married son, so he married her off and gave away a son to him who had another son. A young girl. The man asked her after he entered her: Whose son are you? She said: The son of the girl, meaning so-and-so, and he said: She married to your father his daughter, the son of the woman, so they went to Muawiyah bin Abu Sufyan, and he said: A woman for a woman, and he asked those around him from the people of Syria, and he said: A woman for a woman, so the man said: To Muawiyah, we took it to Ali bin Abi Talib, and he said: Go to him. So they went to Ali, and Ali raised something from the ground. He said: Making up for this matter is easier than that, because this woman was led to do so because of what she permitted from her private parts, and her father must refuse. Prepare the other with what you were led to by this one, and do not approach it until the number of this other one has been completed. He said: And I think he was flogged. He rejected her, or wanted to flog her."
"16618","(16618) Ali bin Musir and Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin al-Mughirah al-Taifi, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman Ibn al-Bilamani, the servant of Omar, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, delivered a speech and said: Marry the young women among you, so he stood up A man came to him and said: O Messenger of God, what are the relations between them? He said: Whatever their families agree upon.

(Bayhaqi 239. Ibn Adi 2188)"
"16619","(16619) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Labib, on the authority of his grandfather, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Who He made it permissible for a dirham, so he made it permissible. He said: And I heard a man giving a fatwa to him, saying: He will marry her for a dirham. (Abu Ali 939)"
"16620","(16420) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Asim bin Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Aamir bin Rabi’ah, on the authority of His father, that a man got married at the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, wearing two sandals, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, permitted it. May his marriage be blessed. (Tirmidhi 1113. Ahmad 3/445)"
"16621","(16621) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaidah, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Sahl bin Saad that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. A man married a woman on the condition that he teach her a surah from the Qur’an. (Bukhari 2310, Muslim 77)"
"16622","(16622) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ismail ibn Umayyah, on the authority of Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab, who said: If you were satisfied With a whip that was a pony."
"16623","(16623) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of his followers, on the authority of Anas, who said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf married a woman of equal weight. A stone of gold is worth three dirhams and a third."
"16624","(16624) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: Whatever the husband and wife agree upon, it is Maher"
"16625","(16425) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Abdul-Malik, on the authority of Ata’, regarding a man who gets married on ten dirhams. He said: He may Muslims used to marry less than that and more."
"16626","(16626) Ismail Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Salih Ibn Muslim, who said: I said to Al-Sha’bi: A man married a woman for a dirham. He said: It is not suitable except with a garment or something."
"16627","(16427) Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, who said: I asked Al-Hasan: What is the minimum that a man can marry? He said: A stone of gold, or the weight of a stone of gold."
"16628","(16428) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath and Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Abu Al-Ajfa’i Al-Salami, on the authority of Omar, who said: No. Exaggerate in women's dowries, for if she had been honored in this world, or had piety in the sight of God, then the most worthy of her would have been Muhammad. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him and your children. He did not marry any of his daughters, nor did he marry any of his women, except for twelve. Safely (Abu Dawud 2099, Ahmed 1/40)"
"16629","(16629) Zaid bin Harun told us: Ibn Aoun told us, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Abu Al-Ajafa Al-Salami, who said Omar said: Do not exaggerate the truthfulness of women. Then he mentioned something like the hadith of Hafs. (Ibn Majah 1887)"
"16630","(16430) Muhammad bin Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, he said: Muhammad bin Ibrahim narrated to me, he said: It was a friendship. The daughters of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the friendship of his wives is five hundred dirhams. (Abu Dawud 2098 and Abd al-Razzaq 10407)"
"16631","(16631) Sharik Abdullah narrated to us, on the authority of Daoud Al-Zaafiri, on the authority of Al-Sha’abi, who said: Ali said: There is no dowry for less than ten. drama"
"16632","(16632) Waki’ bin Al-Jarrah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Rawwad, on the authority of Nafi’, that Omar forbade more than four hundred women."
"16633","(16633) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of his people, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Abraham, that he disliked getting married for less than Forty, but the arbitrator saw no harm in it."
"16634","(16434) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Abdullah bin Omar, on the authority of Nafi’, who said: Ibn Omar married Safiyah. For four hundred dirhams, so she sent to him, “This is not enough for us.” So he increased it by two hundred dirhams in her lifetime."
"16635","(16435) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, who said: The Sunnah in The marriage contract is twelve and a half uqiyah, which is five hundred dirhams."
"16636","(16436) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Hassan, on the authority of Abu Harun, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, who said: It is not upon the man. It is permissible for him to get married with a little of his wealth, or a lot if they agree and agree."
"16637","(16437) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ayyub ibn Musa, on the authority of Ibn Qusayt, that Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab said: If only he had told the truth A whip would have been permissible for him."
"16638","(16438) Abu Asama narrated to us, saying: Musa bin Abdullah narrated to me, saying: Ishaq bin Abdullah bin Abi Talha narrated to us. Al-Ansari, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, married Sawda bint Zam’a over a house he inherited from one of his wives."
"16639","(16639) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: They hated a man to marry in exchange for dirhams. The two dirhams are like the dowry of a prostitute."
"16640","(16440) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’ba, on the authority of Abu Salama, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: He heard him say: They hated that he should get married. For less than three uqs."
"16641","(16441) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Ibn Sakhbara, on the authority of Al-Qasim, on the authority of Aisha, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The women with the greatest blessings have the easiest provisions. (Ahmad 6/145 Hakim 178)"
"16642","(16442) Zaid bin Harun narrated to us, saying: Yahya bin Saeed narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ibrahim Al-Taymi that Abu Hadrad Al-Aslami sought help from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, regarding the dowry of a woman he had married, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, asked him. May God bless him and grant him peace: How much did you believe her? He said: Two hundred dirhams. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: If you had scooped more water, you would not have added more. (Ahmad 3/448, Tabarani 884)"
"16643","(16443) Abdou bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, that Al-Najashi married the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He greeted the mother of his beloved for four hundred dinars. (Abu Dawud 2100, Ibn Saad 98)"
"16644","(16444) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham bin Saad, on the authority of Ata’ al-Khurasani, that Omar married Umm Kulthum at the age of forty. A thousand dirhams."
"16645","(16445) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid told us, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Abi Layla that Abdul Rahman Ibn Awf married a woman for thirty thousand."
"16646","(16446) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Umays, on the authority of Al-Mughirah ibn Hakim, who said: The first to institute zadaq were four. One hundred dinars Omar bin Abdul Aziz."
"16647","(16447) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; He married Shumaila Al-Salamiyya on ten thousand."
"16648","(16448) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, that Ibn Umar used to marry one of his daughters to Ali. Ten thousand

(Abu Yusuf 1021)"
"16649","(16449) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Mahdi, on the authority of Ghaylan, on the authority of Mutarrif, that he was the most truthful woman who married his children. Aqeel twenty thousand."
"16650","(16450) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, that Omar permitted a woman to believe two thousand and permitted Othman in four thousand."
"16651","(16451) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Kurayb bin Hisham, and he was one of the companions of Abdullah said that he married a woman for four thousand."
"16652","(16452) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abu Hilal, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: Amr bin Harith proposed to Adi bin Hatim. His daughter, but he refused except to follow his ruling, so Adi ruled according to the Sunnah of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, over eighty-four hundred years, so he sent Amr came to him with ten thousand, and he said: Prepare it."
"16653","(16453) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Muhammad, that Al-Hasan bin Ali married a woman and sent to her a hundred A female slave, with each female slave a thousand dirhams."
"16654","(16454) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that a man married a woman and he was pleased with that, but he differed. She was in her house, and a neighbor of hers saw her entering, so he threw her at her, so he disputed with him to Omar bin Al-Khattab, and said: The Commander of the Believers, he used to go in on a slave girl and I did not know whether he married her, so he said to him: What do you say? He said: I married a woman for something less and I hid that. He said: Who is your witness? He said: She brought some of her family to witness. He said: Then the punishment turned away from Qadfih and said: Announce this marriage and guard these private parts."
"16655","(16455) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hammad ibn Zayd, on the authority of Hisham, who said: My father used to say: A secret marriage is not valid."
"16656","(16456) Zaid bin Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud bin Qais, who said: I heard Nafi’, the client of Ibn Umar, saying: It is not in Islam. Secret sex"
"16657","(16457) Abu Nu’aym told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ziyad ibn Fayyad, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Utba, who said, The most evil marriage is marriage. The secret"
"16658","(16458) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, passed by a bride, and he said: If only he had fun with this. (Bukhari 5162, Hakim 184)"
"16659","(16659) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: I was informed that if Omar heard a voice he would disavow it. He asked about it, and if it was said about a wedding or circumcision, he agreed with it."
"16660","(16460) Waki’ bin Al-Jarrah narrated to us, on the authority of Usama bin Zayd, on the authority of a sheikh from Banu Salama, on the authority of Abu Qatada that he said To a maid at a wedding beating the tambourine: “Take care of yourself, take care of yourself.”"
"16661","(16461) Ismail bin Ayash told us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr bin Ata, on the authority of Abi Salamah bin Abdul Rahman said: The tambourine was played on the night of the King and it was sung on the head of Abdul Rahman bin Awf."
"16662","(16662) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Aamir bin Saad, who said: I entered upon Abu Masoud and Qarza bin Ka’b. And when they were singing, I said: Are you doing this when you are the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? He said: He said: He gave us permission to have fun at the wedding. (Bayhaqi 289. Tabarani 690)"
"16663","(16663) He told us his youth, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Abu Balaj, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Hatib, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: The sound separates what is permissible from what is forbidden. The sound means beating the tambourine. (Tirmidhi 1088 and Ahmad 3/418)"
"16664","(16644) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, he said: I heard Abu Ishaq narrating, on the authority of Aamir bin Saad, that he said: I was with Thabit Ibn Wadi'a and Qarza' Ibn Ka'b were at a wedding, and I heard the sound of singing, so I said: Aren't you listening? They said: Indeed, we have been given permission to sing at the wedding and to cry over the dead without moaning. (Hakim 184, Tayalisi 1221)"
"16665","(16465) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, saying: Ibn Aoun narrated to us, saying: There was an angel in the family of Muhammad, so when they had finished and Muhammad returned to His house. He said to them: Where is your cuff? Ibn Aoun said: He means the tambourine."
"16666","(16666) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of a man who said: Ibn Masoud entered a wedding party there. Psalms and amusement, so he sat and did not stop."
"16667","(16667) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; When he circumcised his sons, he called the players and gave them four dirhams, or he said: three."
"16668","(16668) Ibn Fudail told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Mughra’ Al-Amma, on the authority of Shurayh that he heard the sound of a tambourine, He said: Angels do not enter a house in which there is a tambourine."
"16669","(16669) Yahya bin Saeed and Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Imran bin Muslim, he said: He said to me Khaythamiya: Did you not hear Suwaid say: Angels do not enter a house in which there is a tambourine."
"16670","(16670) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The companions of Abdullah You will meet the maidservants in the middle, carrying the duff, and split them in pieces."
"16671","Abu Abd al-Rahman Buqi bin Mukhlid narrated to us, saying: Abu Bakr narrated to us, saying:

(16671) Abu Bakr bin Ayash told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Al-Qasim, that Abdullah bin Ja’far brought his two sons together, Ali. And his wife, meaning someone else."
"16672","(16672) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Ikrimah ibn Khalid, that Abdullah ibn Safwan married a woman. A man from Thaqif and his daughter, i.e., from someone else."
"16673","(16673) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub: Muhammad Ibn Sirin was asked about that, but he did not see any harm in it, and he said: I was informed that It was created by a man who lived in Egypt and married the mother of a man’s son and his daughter, meaning someone else."
"16674","(16474) Al-Thaqafi narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, who said: I was informed, on the authority of Saad bin Qurah, a man from the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. Bringing a man together with a woman and another woman’s daughter."
"16675","(16475) Abd al-Salam told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of al-Sha’bi, who said: There is no harm for a man to have intercourse between the mother of a man’s son and his daughter. That means other than that."
"16676","(16676) Abdul Salam told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: There is no harm for a man to have intercourse between his wife and his daughter. That means other than that."
"16677","(16677) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: There is no harm in a man bringing together the man’s two sons. And her father's wife, and Al-Hassan hated him."
"16678","(16678) Ibn Aliya told us, on the authority of Salama bin Alqamah, who said: Al-Hasan was asked about that, and he thought about it, and some of them said to him: : O Abu Saeed, do you see anything between them? He looked and said: I don't see anything between them."
"16679","(16679) Shababi told us, on the authority of Laith bin Saad, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Suleiman bin Yasar that He used to say: There is no harm in a man having intercourse between a woman and his father’s wife."
"16680","(16680) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, who said: I asked Muhammad, and he said, I do not know of any harm in him."
"16681","(16681) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, who said: Al-Hasan was asked about a man who marries another man’s wife and his daughter, so he thought. That means other than it."
"16682","(16682) He told us his youth, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Fudail, on the authority of Abu Hariz, on the authority of Ikrimah that he used to hate it. That a man unites a woman with her father’s wife."
"16683","(16483) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Uthaym, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abd al-Rahman al-Bilamani, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Umar He said: The Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked: What is permissible in breastfeeding from among the witnesses? A man and a woman said.

(Ahmad 2/109 Bayhaqi 464)"
"16684","(16484) Issa bin Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Omar bin Saeed bin Abi Hussein, who said: Abdullah bin Abi narrated to me. Your king, he said: Uqba bin Al-Harith told me, he said: I married his son Abu Ihab Al-Tamimi, and when it was early morning Her queen, a female servant of the people of Mecca, came and said: I have breastfed you both, so he rode his heel to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. While he was in Medina, this was mentioned to him, and she had asked the family of the maid but they denied it, so he said: How is it? It had been said, so he left her. And she married other women.

(Bukhari 88, Abu Dawud 3598)"
"16685","(16485) Abdou bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Jabir bin Zaid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: If it was If a woman is satisfied, her testimony regarding breastfeeding is permissible, and her oath will be taken."
"16686","(16686) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Ikrimah bin Khalid that Omar rejected a woman’s testimony in Breastfeeding"
"16687","(16487) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hallam ibn Salih, on the authority of Bukair ibn Faid, that a woman came to a man who had married a woman. She claimed that she had breastfed them, so he came to Ali and asked him, and he said: This is your wife, no one makes her forbidden to you, even if I took a walk and it was better. He asked Ibn Abbas and he said the same thing."
"16688","(16688), on the authority of Maan bin Issa, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: I was informed that a woman came in the time of Uthman She went to her family and said: I have breastfed you. Then he separated them."
"16689","(16689) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, who said: The judges used to differentiate between the men. And his wife is the witness of women regarding breastfeeding."
"16690","(16690) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: A sane woman’s witness is permissible in Breastfeeding"
"16691","(16691) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Talha, on the authority of Khaythami, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, got married May God bless him and grant him peace, a man from among the Muslims who had nothing to do with him, so he commanded his wife to enter upon him, and that man became After the nobles of the Muslims. (Abu Dawud 2121; Ibn Majah 1992)"
"16692","(16692) Abu Bakr told us, on the authority of Abu Muawiyah, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Rukin, on the authority of his father, who said: So-and-so married Ibn Haram was Layla bint Al-Ajama’i during the time of Omar, so he went in with her and did not give her anything of her friendship."
"16693","(16693) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Kurayb bin Hisham, and he was one of the companions of Abdullah said that he married a woman for four thousand, then he consummated the marriage with her before giving her some of her friendship."
"16694","(16694) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab, who said: The people of Medina disagreed about him. And among them were those who disliked it, and among them were those who permitted it, and whichever of them did it, there is no problem."
"16695","(16695) Abdī narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Arouba, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab, who said: If it is We do not see anything wrong with that."
"16696","(16696) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: There is no harm in him."
"16697","(16697) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ali bin Al-Mubarak, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Ikrimah; When Ali wanted to build a building with Fatima, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: Offer something."
"16698","(16698) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Abu Hamza, who said: I witnessed Ibn Abbas and a man ask him that he had married a woman but it was difficult. On the authority of her friendship, Ibn Abbas said to him: If you find nothing but your sandals, give them to her and then go in with them."
"16699","(16699) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Khusayf, on the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr, who said: He may give her, even if it is veil."
"16700","(16700) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: He used to say: He would throw even a garment over her, then enter. With it"
"16701","(16701) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan and Mansur, on the authority of Ibrahim, that they were That he consummated the marriage with her without giving her anything from her friendship."
"16702","(16702) Zayd ibn Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Dahhak ibn Uthman, who said: Al-Zuhri was asked about a man who married a woman and he Full of her friends, should he enter into her without giving her anything? He said: The Sunnah is that he should not have intercourse with her until he gives her even something."
"16703","(16703) Abdī narrated to us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of his leaders, who said: He will guide something."
"16704","(16704) Shababah narrated to us, saying: Hisham ibn al-Ghaz narrated to us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: It is not permissible for a Muslim to enter upon me. A woman until he presents to her, whether small or large."
"16705","(16705) Ibn Aliya told us, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Ikrimah; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to Ali: Give her your Hutami armor. (Abdul Razzaq 10429. Ahmad 1/80)"
"16706","(16706) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Yazid bin Jabir, on the authority of Ismail bin Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Abdul Al-Rahman bin Ghanam, on the authority of Omar, said: She has a condition. A man said: Then we should be divorced. Omar said: The rights are severable according to the condition."
"16707","(16707) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abdul Aziz, on the authority of Ismail bin Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Ibn Ghanam, on the authority of Omar, who said: She has no condition."
"16708","(16708) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abd al-Hamid ibn Ja’far, on the authority of Yazid ibn Abi Habib, on the authority of Abu al-Khair, On the authority of Uqba bin Amir, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The most deserving condition is that what you have made permissible be fulfilled. broiler

(Bukhari 5151, Abu Dawud 2132)"
"16709","(16709) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, that Muawiyah asked about her. Amr bin Al-Aas, and he said: It has its condition."
"16710","(16710) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Abu Al-Sha’tha’i, who said: If he stipulates for her a home, then it is what he deems permissible. From her relief"
"16711","(16711) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hayyan, who said: Abu Al-Zannad narrated to us that a woman quarreled with her husband to Omar bin Abdul Aziz had stipulated that she should have a home when he married her, and he wanted to take her out of it, so Omar decided that she should have a home, no He took her out of it and said: By the One in whose hand is Omar’s soul, if she were to remove her private parts from the fornication of someone with gold, I would take what was in her possession."
"16712","(16712) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Isa bin Hattan, on the authority of Mujahid, and Sa`id bin Jubayr. They said: He will take her out, and Yahya bin Al-Jazzar said: So with what thing is it permissible to break free, then with what such-and-such and such-and-such returned?"
"16713","(16713) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Al-Manhal, on the authority of Abbad bin Abdullah, on the authority of Ali bin Abu Talib, regarding the woman whose home was stipulated for her, said: God’s condition came before her condition."
"16714","(16714) Ibn Mubarak narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Harith Ibn Abd al-Rahman Ibn Abi Dhubab, on the authority of Muslim Ibn Yasar, on the authority of Sa’id Ibn Al-Musayyab about a man who marries a woman and stipulates that she should have her own home. He said: He takes her out if he wishes."
"16715","(16715) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Muhammad bin Sirin, on the authority of Shurayh that a woman came and said: He made a condition for her to have her home, and he said: God’s condition before her condition."
"16716","(16716) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim and Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan. They said: He will bring it out if He wills."
"16717","(16717) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Ibn Salem, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi. He said: He can take it wherever he wants, and the condition is invalid."
"16718","(16718) Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Muhammad, regarding a man who married a woman and stipulated a home for her. He said: There is no condition for her."
"16719","(16719) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Habib ibn Jariyah, who said: I heard a peacock being asked about a man who proposed to a woman and stipulated that He has certain things, he said: The condition is nothing."
"16720","(16720) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, that a man married off his daughter for a thousand dinars, and stipulated for himself a thousand. One dinar, so Omar bin Abdul Aziz ruled for two thousand dinars for the woman, not the father."
"16721","(16721) Ibn Aliya told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: If he is the one being married, then he is his."
"16722","(16722) Al-Thaqafi narrated to us, on the authority of Muthanna, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of Urwah and Sa’id, who said: Whichever woman is, she is married. If he has a friend or a friend of hers before the marriage contract, then he is hers, and if he was a lover of hers, then he is hers. Oh God!"
"16723","(16723) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, that Masruq married his daughter in marriage and stipulated that her husband be ten thousand in addition to the dowry."
"16724","(16724) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, he said: I heard Al-Zuhri saying: For a woman what is permissible for her to have intercourse with her."
"16725","(16725), on the authority of Al-Dahhak ibn Al-Mukhlid, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: He did not stipulate any boyfriends for her brother or father. It is more deserving of it if you speak about it."
"16726","(16726) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab that Rafi’ bin Khadij had a girl Muhammad bin Muslima thought about her matter, either because he was arrogant or jealous, so he wanted to divorce her, so she said: Do not divorce me, swear Whatever you wish, the Sunnah was broken with that, and it was revealed: {And if a woman fears disobedience or turning away from her husband} (Tabarani 3091 Hakim 308)"
"16727","(16727) Abdā narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha: {And if a woman feared disobedience or rejection from her husband} The verse said: It was revealed about a woman. She is with a man and his companionship with her is prolonged and he wants to divorce her, but she says: Do not divorce me. And detain me while you are free from me, and these verses were revealed about them. (Bukhari 2450, Muslim 2316)"
"16728","(16728) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Harb Ibn Shaddad, on the authority of Yahya Ibn Abi Kathir, who said: Abu Al-Najashi narrated to us. The servant of Rafi’ bin Khadij: Rafi’ bin Khadij married a woman to his wife, and he said to his first wife: If you wish, I will keep you and not swear to you, and if you wish, I will divorce you. She chose that he should keep her and he would not divorce her."
"16729","(16729) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Harb Ibn Shaddad, on the authority of Yahya Ibn Abi Kathir, on the authority of Muhammad Ibn Ibrahim. Bin Al-Harith, that the daughter of Abdullah bin Ja’far was married to a man from Quraysh, and he gave her a choice between keeping her and not dividing He made it clear that he would divorce her, so she chose for him to keep her and not divorce her."
"16730","(16730) Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Muhammad, on the authority of Ubaidah. He said: I asked him about these verses: {And if A woman who fears disobedience or abandonment from her husband. He said: He is a man who has a wife free of her arrows, so he makes peace with her. He has a right over something, and he is entitled to what she is pleased with, but if she dislikes it, he has the right to make amends to her, or satisfy her with what is due to her. Or he divorces her."
"16731","(16731) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Khalid bin Arara, on the authority of Ali, who said: A man came to him to ask for a fatwa. Concerning {a woman who fears disobedience or abandonment from her husband}, and He said: This is a woman who is with a man, and her eyes escape from her darkness. Or her poverty, or her bad character and she hates parting with him, then if she sets aside for him any of her dowry, it is permissible for him, and if she makes of Her days are nothing, so there is no problem."
"16732","(16732) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwah, on the authority of his father, that Suda when she became old and went to sleep on her day For Aisha until she met God."
"16733","(16733) Uqba bin Khalid narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, the same thing."
"16734","(16734) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Razin, in the Almighty’s saying: {You may put your hope in whomsoever you please among them, and you may seek refuge in yourself. Whomever You wish} was among those who sheltered Aisha, Umm Salama, Zainab, and Hafsa, so their portion of themselves and their wealth was equal to them. Among those whom he hoped for were Sawda, Juwayriyah, Umm Habiba, Maimunah, and Safiyya, so he used to swear to them whatever he wanted. And he wanted to separate from them, so they said to him: Divide to us from yourself whatever you wish and let us be as we are. (Ibn Jarir 25)"
"16735","(16735) Abdul Salam told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, that a woman took possession of seven dirhams from her husband, so he was asked. Misra, about that, said: It was forbidden to him, and I do not know from where it was permissible for him? So I met Al-Sha’bi and asked him, and he said: Meet Abu Bakr bin Abi Musa and ask him, and he is a judge at that time, so I came to him and asked him. He said: If you cannot do something, then let him do what you can. So I went to Al-Sha’abi and mentioned that to him. He laughed and said: Go to Abdullah bin Abdullah bin Utbah, so I went to him and asked him, and he said, “It was forbidden to him,” so I said, “Where is it permissible for him?” He said: Give it away, or emancipate it, or sell it. So I went back to Ash-Sha’bi and asked him, and he said: Go back to him and ask him: Will you observe the waiting period for him? So I went to him, and he said: No, it is his water. So I returned to Al-Shu’bi and informed him, and he said: He agreed with the fatwa, so I went to Ibn Maqil. So I asked him, and Abdul Salam said: I did not remember what he said, so Ammar bin Ruzaq told me, on the authority of Ata bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Ibn Maqil. He said: They come together for marriage."
"16736","(16736) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, who said: I asked Misra about a woman who inherited something from her husband. He said: It was forbidden to him."
"16737","(16737) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Abraham, regarding a woman who took possession of something from her husband, and he said: She was forbidden. Only if you free him once you take possession of him."
"16738","(16738) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughirah, that Ubayd Allah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah said this."
"16739","(16739) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’, that he said: It was forbidden to him."
"16740","(16740) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: She has been forbidden to him, so let him resume his marriage with her if he wants."
"16741","(16741) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, who said: Al-Sha’bi said that."
"16742","(16742) Zayd bin Hubab told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Abd Rabbuh, on the authority of Tawoos, that he was asked about a woman. There was a trap in her husband, so she freed him as soon as she took control of him. He said: If the power of a fly were to separate them, he said:"
"16743","(16743) Hammad bin Khaled told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: It was forbidden to him."
"16744","(16744) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, he said: I asked Al-Hakam and Hammad about a woman inheriting a share from her husband. They said: She is forbidden to him, and if he marries her, she has three divorces."
"16745","(16745) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If he is freed after he marries her, then she is upon him. Three divorces that did not constitute a divorce."
"16746","(16746) Ishaq bin Mansour narrated to us, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Misra, on the authority of Ali, who said: It was forbidden. Aliyah"
"16747","(16747) Al-Thaqafi narrated to us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Muhammad, regarding a woman’s possession of her husband. He said: If she frees him from her place, then they are On their marriage."
"16748","(16748) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If the slave has a free woman and she dies He is the master of a slave, and his wife inherits a share from him, and if she emancipates him in her place, then they are on the basis of their first marriage, and if not Her emancipation was forbidden to him."
"16749","(16749) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Khaled bin Kathir, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, on the authority of Ali, who said: It will be postponed for a year, and if it continues, otherwise it will be separated between them, then they will seek God’s bounty and help from the curse."
"16750","(16750) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Rukān, on the authority of his father and Husayn ibn Qubaysiḥ, on the authority of Abdullah He said: The impotence will be postponed for a year if he has intercourse, otherwise he will separate them."
"16751","(16751) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Rukān, on the authority of Abu Hanzali Al-Nu’man, on the authority of Al-Mughirā ibn Shu’bā. He postponed the curse for a year."
"16752","(16752) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Omar, who said: The curse is postponed for a year, and if he reaches it, Otherwise, it will separate them."
"16753","(16753) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Salem, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, that Omar bin Al-Khattab wrote to Shurayh to postpone The curse is one year from the day it will be raised to it."
"16754","(16754) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Al-Mughirah, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, that Al-Harith bin Abdullah bin Abi Rabi’i appointed a man to leave. For ten months he did not reach his family."
"16755","(16755) Jarir narrated to us on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If a man does not have intercourse with his wife for a period of one or ten years More months"
"16756","(16756) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan and Al-Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim. They said: The cursed person will be postponed from On the day it will be brought to the authority, Yunus said, on the authority of Al-Hasan: It will be postponed for a year, and Mughirah said, on the authority of Abraham: I will not keep the time. But it will be postponed from the day it is brought to the authority."
"16757","(16757) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amer Al-Sha’bi, that he used to say what the companions of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace: The old man will be deferred for a year."
"16758","(16758) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Abdul-Malik, on the authority of Ata’, who said: The curse is postponed for a year, and if he reaches it, Otherwise, it will separate them."
"16759","(16759) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: He will receive it from the day of his dispute over the years."
"16760","(16760) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his followers, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab, who said: The blind and the It is taken, on the authority of his wife, according to his age."
"16761","(16761) Hafs told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The curse is postponed for a year and if he reaches it, otherwise he is separated. Between them."
"16762","(16762) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of some of their sheikhs, that Abu Halimah Muadh Al-Qari His son Harithah ibn al-Nu`man al-Ansari married but did not marry her, so he postponed his life for a year. Yahya said: Then Abd informed me. Al-Rahman Al-Ansari said that when a year had passed, he separated them and said: Praise be to God who spared his daughter Harithah."
"16763","(16763) Zayd ibn Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab, on the authority of Omar, that he postponed The old man"
"16764","(16744) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, that Omar ibn Al-Khattab used to say: It should be postponed for a year. I will not know him except from the day he is raised to authority."
"16765","(16745) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Nasir, who said: I was with Abd al-Malik ibn Marwan, and he came. With two eyes, then, behold, a blind man, and he delayed it for a year."
"16766","(16766) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Shimr, on the authority of Ash-Sha’bi, who said: The curse is postponed for a year."
"16767","(16767) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Salem, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi and Ubaidah, on the authority of Ibrahim. They said: He made a choice at the beginning of the year. If she wants, she can stay, and if she wants, she can leave him."
"16768","(16768) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Salim, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Shuraih, who said: Omar wrote to me to postpone him. If he is able to do so, he may give her the choice, and if she wishes, she may stay, and if she wishes, she may leave him."
"16769","(16769) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The curse will be postponed for a certain period, if it arrives. Otherwise, it is given the choice, then She chose him, so she has no choice after that."
"16770","(16770) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Aroub, on the authority of his followers, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Omar, He deferred the two curses for a year, and if he gave her, otherwise he would separate them, and the friendship is due to her in full."
"16771","(16771) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ash-Shu’bi, on the authority of Shurayh that he used to say about the two eyes if the He reaches his wife: He owes half the sadaq."
"16772","(16772) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Zakah is due upon him."
"16773","(16773) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: She has the dowry."
"16774","(16774) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id bin al-Musayyab and al-Hasan. They said: He gave him a period of life for a year. If he connects, otherwise they will be separated, and the friendship will be due to her."
"16775","(16775) Abdul-A’la told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab, who said: She has the right to dowry."
"16776","(16776) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Hammad ibn Salamah, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwah, on the authority of his father, who said: She has the gift of friendship."
"16777","(16777) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Zam’i, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, who said: She is entitled to half the sadaq."
"16778","(16778) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said, “When he reached her, he passed by her and did not separate them.”"
"16779","(16779) Abd al-A’la narrated to us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri, who said: If he controls her, he will never pass by his wife."
"16780","(16780) Omar told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: If something happens to her, then neither she nor her opponents will speak."
"16781","(16781) Omar told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Amr ibn Dinar, who said: We still hear that if a woman befalls her, then do not Her words and those of her opponents."
"16782","(16782) Omar told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, who said: When a woman befalls her, she has no words or words. Your opponents"
"16783","(16783) Muhammad bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Ala’, on the authority of his leaders and Abu Hashim, who said: If he marries her and then He had intercourse with her once and then was not able to have intercourse with her, so she had no choice after that woman."
"16784","(16784) Muhammad bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Ubaidah, on the authority of Abraham, who said: If he has intercourse with her once, she has no choice."
"16785","(16785) Hakam al-Razi told us, on the authority of Khalil ibn Zurara, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of al-Sha’bi, who said: Whoever marries an immoral person has cut off his marriage. Have mercy on him"
"16786","(16786) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Ibn al-Musayyab, Sulayman bin Yasar, and al-Hasan, And Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, said: She has no choice over the free woman."
"16787","(16787) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: I said to him: Does she have a choice over a free man? He said: No."
"16788","(16788) Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalabi, who said: She has no choice over a free man, and she has no choice over a slave."
"16789","(16789) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he used to say: The slave woman has no choice if she is emancipated. Her husband is free."
"16790","(16790) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, on the authority of Nafi’, that Safiyya bint Abi Ubaid had A slave, and she married him to her slave girl, a virgin, and she hated her husband, and she wanted to emancipate her, so she feared that she would be emancipated. Then she separates from her husband and frees the slave, and if the emancipation is proven, she frees the child after that."
"16791","(16791) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, that she bought Barira So she was freed, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave her a choice, and she had a free husband. (Bukhari 6751, Abu Dawud 2228)"
"16792","(16792) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, who said: Make a choice, even if she is under a man from Quraysh."
"16793","(16793) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: She has the choice whether her husband is free, or A slave"
"16794","(16794) Hafs told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: She was given the choice of a free woman, whether her husband, or a slave."
"16795","(16795) Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith narrated to us, on the authority of Harb ibn Abi al-Aliyah, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid said: She has the choice, even if she is under the Commander of the Faithful."
"16796","(16796) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Al-Hasan ibn Muslim, on the authority of Tawoos, said: She has the choice over the freeman and the slave."
"16797","(16797) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, in the Mamluks, you are under the slave So she was freed. He said: She has the choice as long as he does not touch her."
"16798","(16798) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Hanzala, who said: I heard Tawoos being asked about slave women being freed when they have a free husband of their choice? He said: I have no knowledge, but if she was under a slave she would be given the choice."
"16799","(16799) Abdou narrated to us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: He gave the choice of a free man, whether her husband, or a slave."
"16800","(16800) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Abu Qalab, on the authority of Omar, who said: If the mother is freed, she has the choice unless Her husband had intercourse with her."
"16801","(16801) Abd Allah narrated to us, on the authority of Abd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: If he approaches her, she has no choice, she has accepted."
"16802","(16802) Abdou narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, that Hafsiya, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was freed. A maid of hers, and she said: If your husband has intercourse with you, you have no choice."
"16803","(16803) Abdou narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sulaiman bin Yassar, who said: If her husband cheats on her, then no A choice for her."
"16804","(16804) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalab and Nafi’, who said: She has the choice as long as he does not deceive her."
"16805","(16805) Abd al-Salam narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If the mother is freed, she has the choice as long as he does not have intercourse with her. Her husband"
"16806","(16806) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Hammad, who said: If the female slave is freed, then he has intercourse with her while you do not know. She has the choice, so she has the choice. He said: And I was informed, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he used to say that."
"16807","(16807) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, who said: I was informed, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab that he said: She has the choice. He said: If I had authority over him, I would have struck him."
"16808","(16808) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, regarding what was recited to him, he said: And Ibn Umar said: If it happened and you do not know She has the choice if she knows, even if it befalls her a hundred times."
"16809","(16809) Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, who said: I said to Ata’: If a slave woman is freed and he hastens to kill her, he says: Wretched. What did he do? He said: I said: Does she have a choice over a free man? He said: No."
"16810","(16810) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hikam. He said: If he has intercourse with her while she does not know that she has the choice, then she has the choice. If you knew"
"16811","(16811) Hafs told us, on the authority of some of Hammad’s companions, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If he had intercourse with her and she did not know that she had The choice is hers if she knows."
"16812","(16812) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Juwaybir, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, who said: “When he had intercourse with her, she knew that she had a choice.” This is her satisfaction."
"16813","(16813) Hafs told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If her husband has intercourse with her and she knows that she has a choice, then she has no choice. A choice for her."
"16814","(16814) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If he cheated on her before she made her choice, she would swear that she did not She knows that she has a choice, and then she was given a choice if she was under a slave."
"16815","(16815) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, he said: I asked the arbiter about a man who had a wife and was freed. Then he cheated on her after emancipation, and she said: I did not feel that I had a choice. He said: She was asked to swear that she did not know that she had a choice, then He made a choice and asked Hammad, and he said: This is his wife, but do not give her a choice."
"16816","(16816) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, he said: Al-Haytham informed me, on the authority of Hammad, that he said: She must swear that she did not know. She has the choice."
"16817","(16817) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Jabir ibn Zayd, who said in Al-Muttabiyah, he said: He chose."
"16818","(16818) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Firas, on the authority of Amir, who said: The mukatab is given the choice."
"16819","(16819) Abu Bakr bin Ayash told us, on the authority of Mansour and Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If a woman writes, he helps her. Her husband married her, then she was freed, so she had no choice."
"16820","(16820) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, in Al-Mukattabah: She runs while her husband is with her. He said: She has the choice, even if He strived with her."
"16821","(16821) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan and Mansour, on the authority of Al-Hasan and Ata, that they did not see It is difficult to marry off-living women."
"16822","(16822) Ibn Idris narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin that he used to hate marrying narcissistic women, and he used to Al-Hasan sees no harm in him."
"16823","(16823) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Hammad, that he hated him."
"16824","(16824) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Al-Hakam and Hammad regarding a man who married a woman and stipulated for her: What I have apportioned to you of Night or day with which you are satisfied. They said: This is an invalid condition."
"16825","(16825) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: He was being asked about a man who marries a woman. So he stipulated that he would not do such-and-such, and that he would not spend on her except a known thing. He said: It is only the reconciliation that God commanded it after entering, but he hated it."
"16826","(16826) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, saying: Yunus was asked about the condition in marriage, and he said: Al-Hasan did not see any harm in it if It was public, and Ibn Sirin hated it in the beginning and saw nothing wrong with it after that."
"16827","(16827) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, who said: I asked him about a man who has a wife. So he marries a woman and stipulates for this day and for these two days? He said: There is no harm in it."
"16828","(16828) Ismail bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, about a man who married a woman. So they made a condition for him: If I bring her dowry to such-and-such, otherwise there is no marriage between us. Ibn Abbas said: There is no problem with that."
"16829","(16829) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: It is permissible, as if he had made it an oath, and Al-Hasan was He says: The marriage is permissible and the condition is invalid."
"16830","(16830) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Every condition in marriage is nullified by marriage, except divorce."
"16831","(16831) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Amr ibn Qays, on the authority of his grandmother, that her father married a woman to a servant. So she disputed with her father to Shurayh, and he decided for her about the servant and he decided for the woman about the value of the servant."
"16832","(16832) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, about a man who married a woman on the condition that he would free her father, but he did not He has the value of his father. He said: He has the value of his father."
"16833","(16833) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, regarding a man who marries a woman on the condition that he perform Hajj for her. He said it is permissible."
"16834","(16834) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Abu Khaled, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, regarding a man who marries a woman on the condition that He freed her father and did not sell her. He said: She has the same value as her father."
"16835","(16835) Jarir told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Hammad, about a man who married a woman on the condition that she would perform Hajj, then he divorced her before If he enters with it, he said: It has half the amount with which a person can perform Hajj."
"16836","(16836) He narrated to us, on the authority of Abdul-Ala, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: If a man proposes to another man and he marries him but he denies it. On the other, her right is fixed on this half of the sadaq."
"16837","(16837) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, about a man who wrote to his father, or to his master, that He married him off, so he married her off, then he came and disapproved of him. Al-Sha’bi said: If the husband permits the marriage, then it is permissible, but if he does not permit it. It is nothing and there is no dowry owed to either of them if he had not entered into it."
"16838","(16838) Al-Dahhak bin Mukhlid told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, regarding a man who married his father while he was absent, and he did not consent. The father said: The dowry is upon the son. If the father marries the son and the son does not consent, then the dowry is upon the father."
"16839","(16839) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Jabir, who said: We used to isolate ourselves while the Qur’an was being revealed (Bukhari 5207. Muslim 137)"
"16840","(16840) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Abu al-Zinad, on the authority of Kharijiyah ibn Zayd, that Zayd used to isolate himself from his female slaves. No"
"16841","(16841) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Ikrimah; That Zaid and Saad were secluded."
"16842","(16842) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Ismail Al-Shaybani that he succeeded Rafi’ ibn Khadij as his wife. So she told him that he or she was isolated from sores so that she would not wash."
"16843","(16843) Abu Bakr bin Ayash narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Zaydah bin Umair, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, in his saying: {Your women are crops for you} He said: Whoever wants to isolate, let him isolate, and whoever wants not to isolate, let him isolate."
"16844","(16844) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Taymiy, on the authority of Yahya bin Abbad, that Khabbab was isolated from... concubines"
"16845","(16845) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya ibn Abi Ishaq, on the authority of Ibn Sa’d - meaning Aamir - that Sa’d was He isolates you."
"16846","(16846) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Regarding isolation: The companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, disagreed about it. He said: Zayd and Anas bin Malik were isolated."
"16847","(16847) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ali bin Mubarak, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Abu Salama that Zaid and Sa`d were They isolate us."
"16848","(16848) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Dahhak bin Uthman, on the authority of Salim Abi Al-Nadr, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Aflah, who said: I married a mother The son of Abu Ayyub, and you told me that Abu Ayyub used to isolate, and the mother of the son of Zaid bin Thabit told me that he was He is isolated from her, and Salem said, on the authority of Aisha, the son of Saad, that Saad used to isolate himself from the mothers of his children."
"16849","(16849) Abdou bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, who said: The Ansar did not see It is difficult to be isolated, and among those who said that were Zaid, Abu Ayyub, and Ubayy."
"16850","(16850) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, that Alqamiya and the companions of Abdullah were They isolate you."
"16851","(16851) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of his father, Ali bin Hussein, that he used to isolate and interpret this. Verse: {And when your Lord took from the children of Adam from their backs their offspring}"
"16852","(16852) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Abu Imran, who said: I heard a woman saying: He was Al-Hasan ibn Ali. He isolates himself from you."
"16853","(16853) Abdi told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Saeed, he was asked about isolation, but he did not see anything wrong with it, and he said: It is your tillage. If you wish, you can give it thirst, and if you wish, you can give it water."
"16854","(16854) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Masoud bin Ali, who said: I said to Ikrimah: Should I be isolated from my two female slaves? He said: It is your tillage, so if you wish, make it thirsty, and if you wish, water it."
"16855","(16855) Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Zabarqan Al-Sarraj, who said: I asked Ibn Maqil about isolation, and he said: He did that. Who is better than me and Saad than you?"
"16856","(16856) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Dhakwan, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Jabir, who said: We used to recite the Qur’an while reciting it. It comes down and we are not forbidden."
"16857","(16857) Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Aoun ibn Abdullah, on the authority of a man, on the authority of his mother, on the authority of Omar’s secret that He was isolated."
"16858","(16858) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, Mis’ar narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Abi Malik, on the authority of Qaz’a, on the authority of Abu Sa’id. Al-Khudri said: This daughter of mine who is in the room is isolated."
"16859","(16859) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of Jabir, who said: A man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, He said: I have a servant who draws water on a watering can of mine, and I am isolated from her. She brought a son, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: God has not destined any soul to be created except that He exists. (Muslim 64. Ibn Majah 89)"
"16860","(16860) Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, who said: Al-Hasan ibn Sa’d informed me, on the authority of Ibn Abi Maliki, that Ibn Abbas was asked About being isolated, he called his maid and said: I was isolated from you yesterday."
"16861","(16861) Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, who said: Abd al-Malik ibn Umair narrated to me, on the authority of Mus’ab ibn Sa’d, that Sa’d was He is isolated from the mother if he fears that she will become pregnant."
"16862","(16862) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, that Abu Bakr and Omar were He hates isolation and orders people to wash from it."
"16863","(16863) Abdou bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, that men from among the immigrants They hated isolation, among them was so-and-so and so-and-so and Othman bin Affan."
"16864","(16864) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Zirr, on the authority of Ali, who said: Isolation is the hidden valley."
"16865","(16865) Kathir ibn Hisham narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far ibn Burqan, who said: Maimun ibn Mihran narrated to us that Ibn Umar bought He was a slave girl to some of his sons, and he said: Why do I not see her getting pregnant? Perhaps you will be separated from her. If I knew that, my back would hurt."
"16866","(16866) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Yazid bin Khumayr, on the authority of Sulaym bin Amir, on the authority of Abu Umamah, on the authority of Al-Azzal said: I did not think that a Muslim would do that.7"
"16867","(16867) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abd al-Wahid al-Maliki, on the authority of Salem in isolation, he said: The hidden one who is promised."
"16868","(16868) Gandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, that he was hated. Isolation"
"16869","(16869) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Mandal bin Ali, on the authority of Ja’far bin Abi Mughirah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abu Al-Dhail, on the authority of Jarir, who said: A man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, you have not finished. There are no polytheists except with certainty, and I am isolated from it. I want to go to the market with it. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: He came as much as he could. (Tabarani 2370, Musnad 1611)"
"16870","(16870) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Taymi, on the authority of Abu Salama ibn Abd Al-Rahman and Abu Umamah bin Sahl on the authority of all of them, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, who said: When we were afflicted by the captivity of Banu Al-Mustaliq We enjoyed the pleasure of women and separated from them. Then he said: I stopped by a female slave in the market of Banu Qaynuqa’. He said: Then a Jewish man passed by me and said: What is this slave girl, O Abu Sa`id? I said: A slave girl of mine to sell. He said: Have you been doing well with her? He said, I said: Yes, he said: Perhaps you will sell her while there is a khala in her belly? He said: I said: I was isolated from her. He said: That little place of promise. He said: I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. So I mentioned that to him, and he said: The Jews lied, the Jews lied. (Nasa’i 9084. Tahawi 32)"
"16871","(16871) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Muhammad bin Yahya bin Hibban, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muhayriz said: Abu Sarmah al-Mazini and I entered and found Abu Sa`id narrating as Abu Salama and Abu Imamam that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The Jews lied, and he said at the end of the hadith: And it is not upon you that you do not do it. God has destined what He is the Creator of His creation until the Day of Resurrection. (Bukhari 4138 and Muslim 127)"
"16872","(16872) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim al-Taymimi and Amr ibn Murā, who said: He should be isolated from the mother. And the heat is controlled."
"16873","(16873) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, a similar story."
"16874","(16874) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Muhammad, the same as him."
"16875","(16875) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Hamid Al-Araj, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: He is not isolated from the heat unless With her permission"
"16876","(16876) Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi and Yazid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hisham al-Dastawai, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Many, on the authority of Siwar al-Kufi, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: The heat is maintained and he is isolated, from the mother."
"16877","(16877) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Hammam, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Jabir ibn Zayd, who said: He is not isolated from the heat except With her permission"
"16878","(16878) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Talha, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Ar-Rabi’, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abi Sa’ad, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, they said: A free woman is allowed to be free, but a female slave is not."
"16879","(16879) Asbat narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’, who said: He was asked about a mother who is separated from her. He said: Yes, but as for The free woman takes her over."
"16880","(16880) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Zam’i, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, that he used to isolate himself from his mothers and did not He says something about the heat."
"16881","(16881) Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, regarding a man who buys virgin mothers. He said: No. They approach what is not related to her until he purifies her."
"16882","(16882) Ibrahim bin Sadiqa told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who bought a virgin maid and said: He will purify her ties of kinship."
"16883","(16883) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Rabi’, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: He will declare her innocent, even if she is a virgin."
"16884","(16884) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ali bin Mubarak, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Ikrimah similar to this."
"16885","(16885) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, about the gift of a man who bought a slave girl between her parents who was a virgin. He said: He will purify her in two menstruation, and if she does not menstruate, then in forty-five days."
"16886","(16886) Abdul Wahhab told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: If he buys a virgin mother, then He will clear her."
"16887","(16887) Abbad ibn al-Awwam narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Makhoul, who said: I said to al-Zuhri: Did you not know that the lifespan until the expiration of His term, and Ibn Masoud was in Iraq until the end of his term, and Othman ibn Affan used to cleanse the mothers with a period until it was Mu'awiyah, and he used to say: Two menstrual cycles, and Al-Zuhri said: And I will add more to you than Ubadah ibn al-Samit."
"16888","(16888) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Firas, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Alqamiya, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: Mothers will be cleansed. During menstruation."
"16889","(16889) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Salah, Quthm, and Najiya, who said: If a man buys his female slave, then do not He brings her closer until she menstruates."
"16890","(16890) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Abd Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, regarding the slave woman who has intercourse, he said: If she is sold Or she is freed, let her be cleansed by her menstruation."
"16891","(16891) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: I asked him about a man who bought a female slave who had a husband. He said: He purifies her womb through her menstruation."
"16892","(16892) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Atiyya, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: Whoever buys a female slave should not marry her. Until he purifies her with her menstruation."
"16893","(16893) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Hassan bin Salih, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: By menstruation."
"16894","(16894) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali, who said: The mother is to be cleansed. During menstruation."
"16895","(16895) Hatim bin Wardan told us, on the authority of Burd, on the authority of Makhoul, who said: If you buy a slave woman, he says: He will purify her with one menstruation."
"16896","(16896) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’ and Tawus, who said: A mother is purified by her menstruation."
"16897","(16897) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Ata’, who said: Omar said: Whoever buys a female slave Let him purify her with menstruation."
"16898","(16898) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan that he used to say: If he bought her while she was menstruating Let him purify her with another menstruation."
"16899","(16899) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If he wishes, he may succumb to this menstrual period."
"16900","(16900) Hisham narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If he buys it from a woman, let him purify her. During menstruation."
"16901","(16901) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: If he buys it from a woman, he will disavow it."
"16902","(16902) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Abu Qalabi, and Ibn Sirin about a man who seeks cleansing of slave women who did not Tahadh said: They did not think that this would become clear in less than three months."
"16903","(16903) Ibn Aliya told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan that he used to say that he would purify her within three months."
"16904","(16904) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’ and Tawus, who said: She is purified when she menstruates, even if she does not menstruate. Three months."
"16905","(16905) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Abraham. He said, “Three months.”"
"16906","(16906) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar and Sufyan, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Three months."
"16907","(16907) Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Sadiqa bin Yassar, on the authority of Omar bin Abdul Aziz, who said: Three More months"
"16908","(16908) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Abu Qalaba, that he used to say about the treatment of mothers. The woman who has not menstruated: forty-five."
"16909","(16909) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hikam. He said, “A month and a half.”"
"16910","(16910) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, who said a month and a half."
"16911","(16911) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Nu’man, on the authority of his followers, and Ata’, who said: A female slave who has not menstruated will be cleansed. In forty-five days."
"16912","(16912) Abdul Rahman bin Muhammad Al-Muharbiy told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Hammad, who said: He will purify her in forty-five days."
"16913","(16913) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Ata’, who said: Omar said: If she does not menstruate, then forty. One day"
"16914","(16914) Abdou bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Saeed, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim They said: A month and a half."
"16915","(16915) Abdī bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id bin al-Musayyab, and on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim, they said: The mother is cleansed with two menstruation if she is menstruating."
"16916","(16916) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’, who said: A mother was given birth with me to be cleaned of cleansing, and she had her menstrual period, then It appeared that she was pregnant, so he was seeking cleanliness with her two menstrual periods."
"16917","(16917) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, he said: Yunus was asked about a man who buys a slave woman, then seeks her health, and takes from her. The kiss and the face? Ibn Sirin said: It is disliked for him to get from her what is forbidden to him from another woman until he purifies her. It is mentioned, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he did not see any harm in kissing."
"16918","(16918) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ali ibn al-Mubarak, on the authority of Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, on the authority of Ikrimah regarding the man He buys the young slave girl, and she is younger than that. He said: There is no harm in him touching her before he purifies her."
"16919","(16919) Zaid bin Hubab told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Iyas bin Muawiyah, about a man who bought a female slave. So young that he can't have intercourse like her? He said: There is no harm in him having intercourse with her, but he does not seek her acquittal."
"16920","(16920) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, that he hated to kiss her until he had cleared her."
"16921","(16921) Zayd ibn Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad ibn Salamah, on the authority of Ali ibn Zayd, on the authority of Ayyub al-Lakhmi, who said: It happened to Ibn Omar, my maid, on the day of her maiden’s mouth, as if there was a silver jug on her neck. He said: He could not let himself begin to kiss her. And the people are watching."
"16922","(16922) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Aslam Al-Manqari, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Ubaid bin Umayr, who said: He sold Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf is a maid of his who used to have intercourse with her before he cleared her, and it appeared that she was pregnant to the man. He bought it and disputed with him to Omar, and Omar said: Did you have sex with her? He said: Yes, he said: So you sold it before you cleared it? He said: Yes. He said: I was not worthy of that. So he called the narrator and they looked at him and joined him."
"16923","(16923) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he used to say: A man will purify his female slave if he sells her. at a price, and if he bought it at a price."
"16924","(16924) Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Kathir bin Nabatah, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: If a man buys the maid of honor, he does not When she reaches menstruation, he may purify her for three months. If he commits adultery with her and wants to sell her, then he may also purify her for three months. More months"
"16925","(16925) Yahya bin Adam told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If he wanted to sell it Let him seek her acquittal."
"16926","(16926) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, regarding a slave woman who has intercourse: if she is sold, or She was given away, or was emancipated, so let her be cleansed by her menstruation."
"16927","(16927) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ibn al-Munkadir, he heard Jabir say: The Jews used to say: If a man has intercourse His wife, in her anus, the child was cross-eyed, so she revealed: “Your women are a tillage for you.” (Bukhari 4528 1058)"
"16928","(16928) Abu Bakr bin Ayash told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Zaydah bin Umair, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, in his saying : (Your women are tillage for you) He said: Whoever wants to be isolated, let him isolate, and whoever wants not to isolate, let him isolate."
"16929","(16929) Al-Thaqafi narrated to us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: He comes to her as a man, standing and sitting, and in every condition. He will come to her as long as he did not have it in her back."
"16930","(16930) Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Abu Salih: {Your women are your tillage, so go to your tillage. If you wish, he said: If you wish, then come to him lying down, and if you wish, then moving, and if you wish, then bless him."
"16931","(16931) Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Zabarqan, on the authority of Abu Razin, who said: I heard him say: {So go to your tillage. If you wish} He said: Before the period of purification, but do not go to them before the menstruation."
"16932","(16932) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Salama bin Nubait, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, regarding his saying: (Your wives are your tillage, so come May you be cleansed as you wish.) He said: Pure other than menstruation."
"16933","(16933) Abd al-Rahman bin Muhammad al-Muharbibi narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, in his saying: (Your women are your tillage, so go to your tillage.) Whatever you wish.) He said: Appearance with a stomach however you wish, except in the anus or menstruation."
"16934","(16934) Qubaysah narrated to us, saying: Sufyan informed us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Uthman bin Khathham, on the authority of Ibn Sabit, on the authority of Hafsa, on the authority of Umm Salamah, who said: When the immigrants came to Medina, they married among the Ansar, and they were obligatory for them, and it was The Ansar do not do that, so one of them said to her husband: Even ask the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. So she was ashamed to ask him, so she asked him? So he called her and recited to her: {Your women are your crops, so come to your crops as you wish}, one time.

(Tirmidhi 2979. Ahmad 6/310)"
"16935","(16935) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Al-Husayn, on the authority of Mara Al-Hamdani, that some Jews met some Muslims He said: Do you come to women and see them? He said: It is as if he hated immorality. He said: So they mentioned that, and these verses were revealed: {Your wives are a tillage for you, so come I will plow with you as you wish} So God permitted the Muslims to have private sexual intercourse with women however they wished, and as many as they wished. With their hands, and if they wish, behind us."
"16936","(16936) Muhammad bin Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Mora: {So go to your tillage however you wish} He said: It was The Jews mock the Muslims for having sexual intercourse with women, so God, Blessed and Most High, revealed: {Your women are a tillage for you, so come I plow you as you wish} in the farms as you wish."
"16937","(16937) Muhammad bin Al-Hasan narrated to us, saying: A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, regarding the Almighty’s saying: {Your women are your crops, so come to your crops as you wish.} He said: He may come to her from between her and behind her, unless It is in the anus"
"16938","(16938) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Issa ibn Sinan, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab, in his saying: {Your wives are plowing land. So come to your tillage as you wish. He said: If you wish, isolate yourself, and if you wish, do not isolate yourself."
"16939","(16939) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ali bin Ali, who said: I heard Al-Hasan saying: The polytheists did not understand what they emphasized. Muslims and say: It is not lawful for you to have intercourse with women except for one reason. Then God Almighty revealed: {So go to your tillage. You wish}"
"16940","(16940) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Khaled ibn Rabah, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: Before the vulva."
"16941","(16941) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hanifa, on the authority of Kathir al-Rammah, on the authority of Abu Dhar` who said: I asked Ibn Umar about His saying: (So go to your tillage as you wish) He said: If you wish, isolated, and if you wish, not isolated."
"16942","(16942) Shababih told us, on the authority of Warqa’, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, in the Almighty’s saying: (So go to your tillage. You wish) He said: Go to the women in every way."
"16943","(16943) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Ikrimah: {Then come to them from where God has commanded you} He said: from where He commanded you to isolate yourself."
"16944","(16944) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Yazid ibn al-Walid, on the authority of Ibrahim {So they came to me from where May God command you. They said: In the private parts."
"16945","(16945) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa told us, on the authority of Uthman ibn Al-Aswad, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: From where God commanded you to You shall isolate yourself from them during menstruation."
"16946","(16946) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail al-Azraq, on the authority of Ibn al-Hanafi: {Then come to them from wherever God has commanded you} He said: By marriage, by lawful."
"16947","(16947) Shababih told us, on the authority of Warqa’, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid: {Then come to me from where you are commanded. God} said: They were commanded to keep away from menstruating women, so go to them from where God has commanded you, when they purify themselves from where they have forbidden them. In our menstruation"
"16948","(16948) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Razin: {Then come to them from where God has commanded you} He said: From the time of purification."
"16949","(16949) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaidah, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Rafi’, on the authority of Ibn Abi Maliki, who said: These verses were revealed: {And you will never be able to do justice between women even if you strive} about Aisha."
"16950","(16950) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Muhammad, on the authority of Ubaidah, who said: Love and intercourse."
"16951","(16951) Saul bin Yusuf narrated to us, on the authority of Amr bin Al-Hassan, who said: Concerning love {so do not incline completely}. He said: in The two cheaters {so leave them as one hanging} He said: Neither a single woman nor a married woman."
"16952","(16952) Ali bin Hassan bin Shaqiq narrated to us, saying: Husayn bin Waqid narrated to us, saying: Yazid the grammarian narrated to us, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, regarding his saying: {So leave it as if it were hanging.} He said: Neither divorced nor married."
"16953","(16953) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Omar said: When they close a door and loosen a veil, or reveal A veil has become obligatory to pay charity."
"16954","(16954) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Umar with something similar, adding something to it: and he was alone with her."
"16955","(16955) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Al-Manhal bin Amr, on the authority of Abbad bin Abdullah, he said: Ali said: : If he loosens a veil over his wife and closes a door, then dowry is obligatory."
"16956","(16956) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Al-Minhal ibn Amr, on the authority of Hayyan ibn Marthad, on the authority of Ali Like him"
"16957","(16957) Abdou bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his followers, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Al-Ahnaf that Omar and Ali said: If he closes a door, Or loosen a veil, then she has the dowry and the waiting period."
"16958","(16958) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu al-Zinad, on the authority of Sulayman bin Yasar that a man married a woman, So he said: Then Marwan sent for Zaid, and he said: She has the full dowry. Marwan said: He is one of those who are not orphaned, so he said to him: Zaid: If she had brought a pregnancy or a child, would you have had the punishment imposed on her?"
"16959","(16959) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Makhoul, who said: A group of the Companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, gathered with Omar And Muadh: If he closes the door and lowers the curtain, then it becomes obligatory to give charity."
"16960","(16960) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Awf, on the authority of Zurara ibn Awfa, who said: I heard him say: The Rightly-Guided Caliphs decided The Mahdi is that whoever closes a door, or loosens a curtain, the dowry is obligatory and the waiting period is obligatory."
"16961","(16961) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, he said: Omar said: If it is relaxed Concealment has necessitated friendship."
"16962","(16962) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Musa bin Ubaidah, who said: Nafi’ bin Jubayr bin Mut’im narrated to me, on the authority of a man from the companions of The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: If he relaxes a curtain, or closes a door, then charity is obligatory."
"16963","(16963) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ja’far al-Ahmar, on the authority of Ata’ ibn al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Abu al-Bakhtari, on the authority of Ali, who said: Then If he closes a door, loosens a curtain, or vacates it, then she will be rewarded with charity."
"16964","(16964) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ibn Salem, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Omar and Ali, who said: If he loosens a curtain, or leaves it, it is obligatory. The dowry and her waiting period."
"16965","(16965) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Matar, on the authority of Hayan, on the authority of Jabir that he said: When he looked at her private parts and then divorced her On her is the dowry and on her is the promise."
"16966","(16966) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: When the doors are opened and the curtains are relaxed The obligation of friendship."
"16967","(16967) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If he saw from her something that is not permissible for anyone else, it is obligatory for her. Al-Sadaq and she is required to fulfill the waiting period."
"16968","(16968) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ali bin Mubarak, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman Ibn Thawban reported that a man had sexual intercourse with his wife on the road and granted her the full lifespan of the dowry."
"16969","(16969) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Hasan bin Saleh, on the authority of Firas, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, who said: She is entitled to half of the dowry. And if he sat between her legs."
"16970","(16970) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: If he divorces before consummation, then he has the right to divorce her. Half of the dowry, even if he has left it."
"16971","(16971) Waka`` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawoos, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: She is entitled to half of the sadaqa."
"16972","(16972) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, that a man said to Shuraih: I married a woman and she stayed I have been with her for eight years, then I divorced her while she was a virgin. He said: She gets half the dowry."
"16973","(16973) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: She is entitled to half of the sadaqa."
"16974","(16974) Abu Bakr told us, on the authority of Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ali, who said: If you lose Her husband is not married until he accepts or until he dies."
"16975","(16975) Abdul-A’la told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Abu Qalabi, who said: She is not allowed to get married until she finds out. May his death be upon him."
"16976","(16976) Jarir told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, about a woman who lost her husband, or the enemy took him. He said: : Be patient, for she is only his wife, and she will be afflicted with what befalls women until her husband comes, or he informs her that He died"
"16977","(16977) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: Do not marry the wife of a missing person until he returns, or He dies"
"16978","(16978) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Amr bin Hani, who said: Jabir bin Zaid was asked about A woman whose husband has been absent from her for a long time and she does not know whether she is dead or alive. He said: Wait until you know whether she is alive or dead."
"16979","(16979) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: Do not marry the wife of a missing person until he comes to her with certainty. The death of her husband."
"16980","(16980) Saul bin Yusuf told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam and Hammad regarding his missing wife. They said: Never get married. Until the news comes to her."
"16981","(16981) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim, the same."
"16982","(16982) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab that Omar ibn al-Khattab and Uthman ibn Affan said: Concerning the missing woman: she should wait for four years and wait for four months and ten days."
"16983","(16983) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Mansour, who said: Mujahid narrated to us regarding the drowning of Al-Minhal bin Amr, on the authority of Ibn Abu Layla, on the authority of Omar Ibn Al-Khattab, who said regarding a missing woman: He waited for four years, then he called his guardian and divorced her. After that, she will wait for four months and ten days."
"16984","(16984) Abu Khalid narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, regarding the deceased between the two Siffins, he said: His wife observes the waiting period. Sunnah"
"16985","(16985) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Yahya bin Ja’dah that a man was smitten by the jinn during the time of Omar. So his wife came to Omar, and he ordered her to wait for four years, then he ordered his guardian after four years to divorce her, then he ordered her To observe the waiting period. When her waiting period ends, she gets married. If her husband comes, she has the choice between her wife and two friends."
"16986","(16986) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab in the deceased between the two Siffins: His wife waited for a year."
"16987","(16987) Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi narrated to us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Abu Nazra, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Layla, who said: She saw Omar Khayyar missing. He married his wife between her and the dowry he brought to her."
"16988","(16988) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab that Omar and Uthman ibn Affan said: Her husband came and gave her a choice between his wife and the first friendship."
"16989","(16989) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, Omar was asked about a man who was absent from his wife and reached her. He died, so she got married, then the first husband came, and Omar said: The first husband is given the choice between friendship and his wife, so if he chooses friendship He leaves her with the other husband, and if he wishes, he chooses his wife and Ali says: She is entitled to dowry for what the other has made permissible of her private parts, and he will separate them. And between her, then she observes the waiting period for three menstrual periods, then returns the first."
"16990","(16990) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, who said: A man came to Abraham and said: He had married a woman who was Her husband was mourned for her. A letter had come from her stating that he was alive, so Abraham said to him: Separate her. When he comes, then if he wishes. He chooses the one who is the most truthful and your wife is as she is, and if he chooses the woman, then if her waiting period from you ends, then he is a wife. The first: And she did not believe in what was permissible from her private parts. He said: Shall I eat with her? He said: Yes, and do not enter upon her until you give her permission."
"16991","(16991) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, he said, narrated to us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Abu al-Malih, on the authority of his son Umair Al-Shaybaniyyah said: I was mourned by my husband, Qandabil, and after him I married Al-Abbas bin Tarif, the brother of Banu Qais. So my first husband came, and we went to Othman while he was besieged. He said: How can I make up the dispute between you when I am in this state? We said: We are satisfied with your decision, so the husband had a choice between friendship and a wife. When Uthman was injured, we went to Ali and told the story. Here is the story: The first husband had a choice between friendship and a wife, so he chose friendship, so he took two thousand from me and two thousand from the other."
"16992","(16992) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’ba, on the authority of Sayyar, on the authority of Shu’bi, who said: The wife of the missing person is the wife of the first."
"16993","(16993) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Omar bin Hamza, he said: I heard Al-Qasim bin Muhammad saying: Ibn Al-Zubair judged us in Their master, her husband had mourned, so she got married, then her husband came, and he decided that her first husband had the choice, if he wanted. His wife, and if he wishes, befriend him. Omar said: Al-Qasim used to say that."
"16994","(16994) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Al-Abbas bin Abdul-Rahman, on the authority of Humaid bin Abdul-Rahman, that Omar gave the best The missing man had married his wife, so he chose the money and gave it to her more recent wife. Hamid said: So I entered upon the woman who This was decided for her, and she said: So I helped my other husband with his child."
"16995","(16995) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim, that Ali said: “He is not a husband.” Mr."
"16996","(16996) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Salem, who said: I heard Al-Sha’bi say: He is not a husband."
"16997","(16997) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, that he used to say: He is not married."
"16998","(16998) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Zaid, who said: He is a husband if he does not want to replace him."
"16999","(16999) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Marwan Al-Asfar, on the authority of Abu Rafi’ that Uthman ibn Affan was asked about that. And Ali and Zayd bin Thabit were with him. He said: Then Othman and Zayd gave permission in that matter, saying: He is a husband. Then Ali stood up angry. He hated what they said."
"17000","(17000) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: He is a husband, says the master."
"17001","(17001) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, he said: I asked Hammad about a man who had a mother under his belt, and he divorced her twice, then Her master cheated on her, will she return to her husband? He thought that"
"17002","(17002) Zayd ibn Harun told us, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Amr ibn Harim, who said: Jabir ibn Zayd was asked about a man She had a woman who was his slave and he divorced her. Then her master pleased her and then left her. Is it permissible for her husband who divorced her? Should he review it? He said: She is not permissible for him until she marries another husband."
"17003","(17003) Abdou narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that Zayd bin Thabit and Al-Zubayr bin Al-Awwam were not He sees harm if a man divorces his wife while she has been divorced twice, then her master cheats on her and does not want to do that. It is deceitful and it is not permissible for her to return to her husband with an engagement."
"17004","(17004) Abduh narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Abraham, regarding a slave woman who divorced her husband. She was divorced twice and then her master cheated on her: She is not permissible for her husband until she marries another husband."
"17005","(17005) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawoos, who said: If he divorces her twice and then the master has intercourse with her, he marries her. I wish"
"17006","(17006) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Al-Zinad, on the authority of Suleiman bin Yassar, on the authority of Zayd bin Thabit that Marwan asked him about his thoughts."
"17007","(17007) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, who said: He should not marry until the end of his marriage. The number of the woman he divorced."
"17008","(17008) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Ubaidah; Concerning a man who divorced his wife and had four wives, he said: It is not permissible for him to marry the fifth until the number of He divorced"
"17009","(17009) Aidh bin Habib narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Ali, who said: He should not marry a fifth person until the end of his period. The number of the woman he divorced."
"17010","(17010) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: He should not marry until his waiting period has passed. The one who divorced, Ataa said: If there is no inheritance between them and there is no recourse against her, then there is no problem for him to marry."
"17011","(17011) Abbad bin Awwam told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’, that he was asked about a man who had four wives. So he divorced one of them three times. Should he marry a fifth? He said: No, until the waiting period of the one he divorced has expired."
"17012","(17012) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: He should not marry until his waiting period has passed. The one who divorced, and Ataa said: If there is no inheritance between them and he has no right to take her back from her, then there is no harm in him getting married."
"17013","(17013) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of al-Hasan that he was reluctant to get married until the end of his life. The number of the woman he divorced."
"17014","(17014) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ali bin Mubarak, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ibrahim Al-Taymiyy said that Utba bin Abi Sufyan had four wives, so he divorced one of them, then he married a fifth before he The waiting period for the one who divorced has expired, so Marwan asked Ibn Abbas, and he said: No, until the waiting period for the one who divorced has expired."
"17015","(17015) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Abu Sadiq, who said: He should not marry a fifth person until his number of days has passed. The one who divorced"
"17016","(17016) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If a man has four wives and he divorces one of them He should not marry a fifth woman until the number of days he divorced has expired. If she dies, then if he wishes, he may marry from that day."
"17017","(17017) Hammad bin Khalid told us, on the authority of Malik bin Anas, on the authority of Rabi’a, on the authority of Al-Qasim and Urwah bin Al-Zubayr that they said: In the He has four wives, so he divorced one of them: he can marry whenever he wants."
"17018","(17018) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ali, that he was asked about a man who divorced his wife and her waiting period did not end. Until he married her sister, then Ali separated them and granted her a dowry for what he had permitted of her private parts and said: The other will complete her waiting period. And he is engaged, and if he consummates the marriage with her, then she is entitled to the full dowry, and she is required to complete the waiting period, and she is to observe the waiting period from him, all of them, each one. Three menstrual periods, and if they are not menstruation, then three months."
"17019","(17019) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Amr ibn Shuaib, who said: A man divorced a woman and then married her sister. He said: Ibn Abbas told Marwan, separate him and her until the waiting period of the woman he divorced expires."
"17020","(17020) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If a man marries a woman, then divorces her, then He married her sister during her waiting period. He said: Their marriage is forbidden, and it will separate them, and there is no dowry for her, nor is he considered an iddah against her."
"17021","(17021) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Zakaria, who said: Amer was asked about a man who married a woman, then divorced her, then married her sister. Concerning her waiting period, he said: He should separate them."
"17022","(17022) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: He used to hate it when he had a wife and he divorced her. Thirdly, he disliked marrying her sister until the waiting period of the woman he divorced had expired."
"17023","(17023) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: A woman should not marry her sister during her ‘iddah."
"17024","(17024) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, that he saw no harm if a man divorced his wife three times. To marry her sister during her waiting period."
"17025","(17025) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Al-Hasan, Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, and Khalas in A man divorced his wife three times while she was pregnant. They said: There is no harm in him marrying her sister during her waiting period. He said: It was Ubaid bin Nudailah was hated until this was mentioned to Al-Hasan, and it was as if it had been removed from him."
"17026","(17026) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said May the peace and blessings of God be upon him: A woman should not be married to her paternal aunt or paternal aunt. (Bukhari 5108, Ahmad 3/338)"
"17027","(17027) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Yaqoub bin Utbah, on the authority of Suleiman bin Saar, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri said that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: A woman should not marry her paternal aunt or paternal paternal aunts."
"17028","(17028) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: No. A woman may be married to her paternal aunt or to her paternal aunt."
"17029","(17029) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan that he said: A woman should not be married to her paternal aunt or to her husband. Her aunt"
"17030","(17030) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: A woman may not be married to her paternal aunt, nor to her paternal aunt, and a paternal aunt may not be married to her brother’s daughter, nor to a paternal uncle. Her sister’s daughter, and the younger should not be married off to the eldest, nor should the eldest be married off to the younger. (Tirmidh 1126. Abu Dawud 2058)"
"17031","(17031) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Do not marry A woman is on her paternal aunt or on her maternal aunt."
"17032","(17032) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, who said: I heard Saeed bin Al-Musayyab saying that it is forbidden to marry A woman has sexual intercourse with her paternal aunt or paternal aunt, or a man has intercourse with a woman in whose womb there is a fetus for someone else. (Malik 21)"
"17033","(17033) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim: A man shall not marry his paternal uncle or her maternal aunt. If he divorces her, he must not marry either of them until her waiting period is over."
"17034","(17034) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Zakariya, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, who said: I asked him about a woman who was married to her maternal aunt. Breastfeeding, he said: It separates them."
